      "es": "# Command 00 - Echo Test Message\n\n- **Command ID:** `00`\n- **Title:** Echo Test Message\n- **PDF Pages:** 134 - 134\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 134 -->\n\n00 - Echo Test Message\nCommand 00 tests the communications link between the host and the HSM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<00#Message#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<00#0000Version#Message#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 00 |\n| 1 | Message | 1 - | The test message to be returned in the response. This field |\n1999 contains 1 - 1999 characters. The following characters are\nnot allowed in the message, #, <, and >.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 00 |\n| 1 | Version | 2 | The HSM software version. |\n| 2 | Message | 1 - | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\n1999\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<00#This is a test.#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<00#000081#This is a test.#>\n```\n\n\n",
