    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 101 - Configure HSM Option\n\n- **Command ID:** `101`\n- **Title:** Configure HSM Option\n- **PDF Pages:** 655 - 657\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 655 -->\n\n101 - Configure HSM Option\nCommand 101 enables and disables various operating parameters. The values defined for these options\nare stored in non-volatile memory. Power cycling the HSM does not change the value of an option.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION: Enabling on option 44 degrades performance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<101#[Option Text]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<201#Y#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 101 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 656 -->\n\n\n### Command description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | [Option Text] | Variable | Option text consists of a three-digit option ID and a one-digit |\naction flag. The length of this field must be zero or a multiple\nof four. When this field is empty, all options will be set to\ntheir default values.\nThe following options are supported:\n020 = Append the 3DES Master File Key name to all\nresponses. The value “MFK0” will be included when\na 3DES Master File Key is not present in the HSM.\nBy default the 3DES MFK name is not appended to\nthe response.\n021 = Append the detailed error code to error responses.\nBy default, the detailed error code is not appended\nto the response.\n023 = Remove the Carriage Return and Line Feed\ncharacters from all responses. By default, they are\nappended to the response.\n027 = Use the rightmost 4 PIN digits for Diebold PIN\nverification. By default, the leftmost 4 PIN digits are\nused.\n044 = Record invalid commands and error responses in\nthe system log. This option has a significant\nperformance impact . By default, the HSM does not\nrecord invalid command and error responses. When\nthis option is enabled, warning messages may\nappear in the system log for certain commands the\nSCA sends to the HSM. This is not an error\ncondition.\nThe following action Flags are supported:\nD = Disable option\nE = Enable option\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 201 |\n| 1 | Y | 1 | The specified configuration change has been implemented. |\nExamples\nSet multiple configuration options\n Append the Master File Key name to the response; indicated by the option text 020E.\n Append detailed error information to response 00; indicated by the option text 021E.\n Use the right-most 4 PIN digits for Diebold PIN verification; indicated by option text 027E\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#020E021E027E#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 657 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nEnable error logging\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#044E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nDisable error logging\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#044D#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nDisable the carriage return and line feed (CRLF)\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#023E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nReset options to their default values\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101##>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 101 - Configure HSM Option\n\n- **Command ID:** `101`\n- **Title:** Configure HSM Option\n- **PDF Pages:** 655 - 657\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 655 -->\n\n101 - Configure HSM Option\nCommand 101 enables and disables various operating parameters. The values defined for these options\nare stored in non-volatile memory. Power cycling the HSM does not change the value of an option.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION: Enabling on option 44 degrades performance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<101#[Option Text]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<201#Y#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 101 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 656 -->\n\n\n### Command description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | [Option Text] | Variable | Option text consists of a three-digit option ID and a one-digit |\naction flag. The length of this field must be zero or a multiple\nof four. When this field is empty, all options will be set to\ntheir default values.\nThe following options are supported:\n020 = Append the 3DES Master File Key name to all\nresponses. The value “MFK0” will be included when\na 3DES Master File Key is not present in the HSM.\nBy default the 3DES MFK name is not appended to\nthe response.\n021 = Append the detailed error code to error responses.\nBy default, the detailed error code is not appended\nto the response.\n023 = Remove the Carriage Return and Line Feed\ncharacters from all responses. By default, they are\nappended to the response.\n027 = Use the rightmost 4 PIN digits for Diebold PIN\nverification. By default, the leftmost 4 PIN digits are\nused.\n044 = Record invalid commands and error responses in\nthe system log. This option has a significant\nperformance impact . By default, the HSM does not\nrecord invalid command and error responses. When\nthis option is enabled, warning messages may\nappear in the system log for certain commands the\nSCA sends to the HSM. This is not an error\ncondition.\nThe following action Flags are supported:\nD = Disable option\nE = Enable option\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 201 |\n| 1 | Y | 1 | The specified configuration change has been implemented. |\nExamples\nSet multiple configuration options\n Append the Master File Key name to the response; indicated by the option text 020E.\n Append detailed error information to response 00; indicated by the option text 021E.\n Use the right-most 4 PIN digits for Diebold PIN verification; indicated by option text 027E\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#020E021E027E#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 657 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nEnable error logging\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#044E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nDisable error logging\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#044D#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nDisable the carriage return and line feed (CRLF)\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101#023E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\nReset options to their default values\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<101##>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<201#Y#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
