    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 105 - Install a license\n\n- **Command ID:** `105`\n- **Title:** Install a license\n- **PDF Pages:** 661 - 662\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 661 -->\n\n105 - Install a license\nThis command license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands, and options in a specific\nHSM/Domain.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<205#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License | Variable | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains |\nhexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible\nby 16.\n| 3 | MAC | 9 | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field |\ncontains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4\nhexadecimal characters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 205 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 11, 12 | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\nMAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate.\nCONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error.\nSN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match\nthe serial number in the command.\n| 2 | Version | 4 | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters. |\n\n\n<!-- Page 662 -->\n\nUsage Notes\n The HSM serial number is required when placing an order for in field scalability features or\ncustomer-specific commands and options. When the order is processed, a Command 105 for that\nspecific HSM serial number will be provided. Be sure you send the Command 105 you receive to the\ncorrect HSM. Field one of the response to Command <9A#ID#> will contain the HSM serial number.\n This command updates non-volatile memory with the configuration. In field scalability features and\ncustomer-specific commands and options are not lost if the HSM is powered off. It is not necessary to\nsend this command each time the HSM is powered on.\n After sending the command 105 to the HSM, you must then use the SCA to add the customer-specific\ncommands and options to HSM’s security policy.\n Resetting the HSM to factory state erases the license.\nExample\n The serial number is 123456.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This example does not enable any additional functionality.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F 3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<205#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 105 - Install a license\n\n- **Command ID:** `105`\n- **Title:** Install a license\n- **PDF Pages:** 661 - 662\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 661 -->\n\n105 - Install a license\nThis command license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands, and options in a specific\nHSM/Domain.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<205#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License | Variable | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains |\nhexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible\nby 16.\n| 3 | MAC | 9 | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field |\ncontains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4\nhexadecimal characters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 205 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 11, 12 | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\nMAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate.\nCONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error.\nSN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match\nthe serial number in the command.\n| 2 | Version | 4 | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters. |\n\n\n<!-- Page 662 -->\n\nUsage Notes\n The HSM serial number is required when placing an order for in field scalability features or\ncustomer-specific commands and options. When the order is processed, a Command 105 for that\nspecific HSM serial number will be provided. Be sure you send the Command 105 you receive to the\ncorrect HSM. Field one of the response to Command <9A#ID#> will contain the HSM serial number.\n This command updates non-volatile memory with the configuration. In field scalability features and\ncustomer-specific commands and options are not lost if the HSM is powered off. It is not necessary to\nsend this command each time the HSM is powered on.\n After sending the command 105 to the HSM, you must then use the SCA to add the customer-specific\ncommands and options to HSM’s security policy.\n Resetting the HSM to factory state erases the license.\nExample\n The serial number is 123456.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This example does not enable any additional functionality.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F 3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<205#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
