      "es": "# Command 107 - Confirm Temporary Serial Number\n\n- **Command ID:** `107`\n- **Title:** Confirm Temporary Serial Number\n- **PDF Pages:** 666 - 667\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 666 -->\n\n107 - Confirm Temporary Serial Number\nCommand 107 implements the temporary serial number you defined with command 106.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA Set Temporary Serial Number feature to install a temporary\n> [!NOTE]\n> serial number.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<107#Encrypted Challenge#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <207#Status#Permanent | Serial | Number#Temporary | Serial Number#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 107 |\n| 1 | Encrypted Challenge | 16, 18 | The result of encrypting or MACing the challenge number |\nreturned in the response to command 106. If the 3DES MFK\nwas used, this field will be the 16-character result of\nencrypting the challenge under variant 30 of the MFK. If the\nAES MFK was used, this field will be the leftmost 18\ncharacters of the CMAC calculated across the challenge.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 207 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 10, | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\n11\nBAD CHALLENGE = the decrypted challenge number is not\ncorrect.\nNO TMP SN = the HSM does not have a challenge number to\ncompare to the challenge number provided in the command.\n| 2 | Permanent Serial | 6 | The HSM permanent serial number. |\nNumber\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\n\n\n<!-- Page 667 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 3 | Temporary Serial | 0, 6 | The temporary serial number installed in the HSM. This field |\nNumber is empty unless response field 1 = COMPLETED.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\nExample\nUsing Command 107 to implement a temporary serial number.\nThis is not a valid example.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<107#B203A98A64C8F906#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<207#COMPLETED#123456#654321#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 107 - Confirm Temporary Serial Number\n\n- **Command ID:** `107`\n- **Title:** Confirm Temporary Serial Number\n- **PDF Pages:** 666 - 667\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 666 -->\n\n107 - Confirm Temporary Serial Number\nCommand 107 implements the temporary serial number you defined with command 106.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA Set Temporary Serial Number feature to install a temporary\n> [!NOTE]\n> serial number.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<107#Encrypted Challenge#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <207#Status#Permanent | Serial | Number#Temporary | Serial Number#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 107 |\n| 1 | Encrypted Challenge | 16, 18 | The result of encrypting or MACing the challenge number |\nreturned in the response to command 106. If the 3DES MFK\nwas used, this field will be the 16-character result of\nencrypting the challenge under variant 30 of the MFK. If the\nAES MFK was used, this field will be the leftmost 18\ncharacters of the CMAC calculated across the challenge.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 207 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 10, | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\n11\nBAD CHALLENGE = the decrypted challenge number is not\ncorrect.\nNO TMP SN = the HSM does not have a challenge number to\ncompare to the challenge number provided in the command.\n| 2 | Permanent Serial | 6 | The HSM permanent serial number. |\nNumber\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\n\n\n<!-- Page 667 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 3 | Temporary Serial | 0, 6 | The temporary serial number installed in the HSM. This field |\nNumber is empty unless response field 1 = COMPLETED.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\nExample\nUsing Command 107 to implement a temporary serial number.\nThis is not a valid example.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<107#B203A98A64C8F906#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<207#COMPLETED#123456#654321#>\n```\n\n\n"
