    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 109 - Confirm Security Policy\n\n- **Command ID:** `109`\n- **Title:** Confirm Security Policy\n- **PDF Pages:** 674 - 675\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 674 -->\n\n109 - Confirm Security Policy\nCommand 109 implements the security policy you defined with command 108.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the\n> [!NOTE]\n> HSM security policy.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<109#[Warning Acknowledgment]#Challenge Response#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<209#Security Policy#Sequence Number#Serial Number#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 109 |\n| 1 | [Warning | 8 | If the security policy, defined in the 108 command, disabled |\nAcknowledgment] both the sequence number and serial number validation,\noptions (6E) and (6F), a warning message “SECURITY\nPRECAUTION: Are you sure?” was included in the 208\nresponse. You must supply the following warning\nacknowledgment message:\nI accept\nbefore the HSM’s security policy will be implemented. This\nfield is not case sensitive. This field is empty if the HSM’s\nsecurity policy does not disable both of these options.\n| 2 | Challenge Response | 32, 36 | The result of encrypting or MACing the left and right |\nchallenge numbers returned in the response to command\n108. If the 3DES MFK was used, this field will be the 32-\ncharacter result of encrypting the challenges under variant\n30 of the MFK. If the AES MFK was used, this field will be\nthe concatenation of two MACs.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 209 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 675 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Security Policy | Variable | The security policy that was just implemented. If the |\nsecurity policy is defined by several command 108\ncommands, this field will only show the security policy for\nthe most recent 108 command. You can use the HSM\nConfiguration Status (Command 9A) to obtain a complete\nlist of commands and options enabled and disabled in the\nHSM.\n| 2 | Sequence Number | 16 | The number of times the security policy has been |\nsuccessfully updated. This value is used in processing of\nthe security policy. It is displayed so you can keep track of\nthe number of times each of your HSM’s security policy has\nbeen updated.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n| 3 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<109##203A98A64C8F900C62E1E8368E43A751#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<209#30=e;90=e;32=e;37=e;(66)=”e”;(A0)=”6”;10=d;30=d;98=d;(65)=d#0000000000000\n```\n\n001#A7PV87#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 109 - Confirm Security Policy\n\n- **Command ID:** `109`\n- **Title:** Confirm Security Policy\n- **PDF Pages:** 674 - 675\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 674 -->\n\n109 - Confirm Security Policy\nCommand 109 implements the security policy you defined with command 108.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is deprecated. Use the SCA HSM Configuration Management feature to configure the\n> [!NOTE]\n> HSM security policy.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<109#[Warning Acknowledgment]#Challenge Response#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<209#Security Policy#Sequence Number#Serial Number#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 109 |\n| 1 | [Warning | 8 | If the security policy, defined in the 108 command, disabled |\nAcknowledgment] both the sequence number and serial number validation,\noptions (6E) and (6F), a warning message “SECURITY\nPRECAUTION: Are you sure?” was included in the 208\nresponse. You must supply the following warning\nacknowledgment message:\nI accept\nbefore the HSM’s security policy will be implemented. This\nfield is not case sensitive. This field is empty if the HSM’s\nsecurity policy does not disable both of these options.\n| 2 | Challenge Response | 32, 36 | The result of encrypting or MACing the left and right |\nchallenge numbers returned in the response to command\n108. If the 3DES MFK was used, this field will be the 32-\ncharacter result of encrypting the challenges under variant\n30 of the MFK. If the AES MFK was used, this field will be\nthe concatenation of two MACs.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 209 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 675 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Security Policy | Variable | The security policy that was just implemented. If the |\nsecurity policy is defined by several command 108\ncommands, this field will only show the security policy for\nthe most recent 108 command. You can use the HSM\nConfiguration Status (Command 9A) to obtain a complete\nlist of commands and options enabled and disabled in the\nHSM.\n| 2 | Sequence Number | 16 | The number of times the security policy has been |\nsuccessfully updated. This value is used in processing of\nthe security policy. It is displayed so you can keep track of\nthe number of times each of your HSM’s security policy has\nbeen updated.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n| 3 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-Z\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<109##203A98A64C8F900C62E1E8368E43A751#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<209#30=e;90=e;32=e;37=e;(66)=”e”;(A0)=”6”;10=d;30=d;98=d;(65)=d#0000000000000\n```\n\n001#A7PV87#>\n\n"
    },
