      "es": "# Command 1101 - HSM Software Version\n\n- **Command ID:** `1101`\n- **Title:** HSM Software Version\n- **PDF Pages:** 1331 - 1331\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1331 -->\n\n1101 - HSM Software Version\nCommand 1101 returns the software image version, image CRC checksum, and the product code.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1101#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <2101#Software | Version#Image | CRC Checksum#Product | Code#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1101 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2101 |\n| 1 | Software Version | Variable | The HSM software version information. |\n| 2 | Image CRC Checksum | 4 | The CRC checksum of the HSM software. |\n| 3 | Product Code | 1 | This field contains a decimal digit, 3 indicates AT1000. |\nUsage Note\nUse command <1100#> to obtain the HSM extended software version information.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1101#>\n```\n\nWhen the HSM is configured with the AKB personality it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2101#Atalla | HSM   AT1000-AKB | Version: | 8.60,   Date:   Jul   15   2024,   Time: |\n16:24:41#FC67#3#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the Variant personality it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2101#Atalla | HSM   AT1000-VAR | Version: | 8.60,   Date:   Jul   15   2024,   Time: |\n16:25:37#11C6#3#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the PCI-HSM personality it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2101#Atalla | HSM   AT1000-AKB | PCI-HSM | Version:   8.60,   Date:   Jul   15   2024,   Time: |\n16:26:40#0551#3#>\n\n",
