      "es": "# Command 1105 - Install a License in all Domains\n\n- **Command ID:** `1105`\n- **Title:** Install a License in all Domains\n- **PDF Pages:** 1334 - 1335\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1334 -->\n\n1105 - Install a License in all Domains\nCommand 1105 simultaneously license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands and\noptions for all domains that are currently configured.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands\n> [!NOTE]\n> and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2105#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License | Variable | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains |\nhexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible\nby 16.\n| 3 | MAC | 9 | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field |\ncontains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4\nhexadecimal characters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2105 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 11, 12 | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\nMAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate.\nCONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error.\nSN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match\nthe serial number in the command.\n| 2 | Version | 4 | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters, which are the |\ncommand version.\nExample\n The serial number is 123456.\n\n\n<!-- Page 1335 -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This is not a valid example.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F 3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2105#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1105 - Install a License in all Domains\n\n- **Command ID:** `1105`\n- **Title:** Install a License in all Domains\n- **PDF Pages:** 1334 - 1335\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1334 -->\n\n1105 - Install a License in all Domains\nCommand 1105 simultaneously license in field scalability features, customer-specific commands and\noptions for all domains that are currently configured.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: After sending the command 1105 to the HSM, use the SCA to enable the customer-specific commands\n> [!NOTE]\n> and options in each of the Domains. This command must be sent to Domain0.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1105#Serial Number#License#MAC#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2105#Status#Version#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1105 |\n| 1 | HSM Serial Number | 6 | The HSM serial number. |\n| 2 | License | Variable | The encrypted form of the license. This field contains |\nhexadecimal characters. The length of this field is divisible\nby 16.\n| 3 | MAC | 9 | The MAC of the serial number and license. This field |\ncontains 4 hexadecimal characters a space and 4\nhexadecimal characters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2105 |\n| 1 | Status | 9, 11, 12 | COMPLETED = the command was successfully processed. |\nMAC MISMATCH = the MAC did not validate.\nCONF INVALID = the decrypted license contained an error.\nSN MISMATCH = the HSM serial number does not match\nthe serial number in the command.\n| 2 | Version | 4 | This field contains 4 hexadecimal characters, which are the |\ncommand version.\nExample\n The serial number is 123456.\n\n\n<!-- Page 1335 -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This is not a valid example.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1105#123456#E7F35DA354A09F32#B65F 3CA0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2105#COMPLETED#VER1#>\n```\n\n\n"
