      "es": "# Command 1110 - HSM System Configuration Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1110`\n- **Title:** HSM System Configuration Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1336 - 1336\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1336 -->\n\n1110 - HSM System Configuration Information\nCommand 1110 returns the HSM system software information, and cryptographic subsystem software\nversion information.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1110#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2110#Software Version Information#Image ID#Image CRC Checksum#\n```\n\nProduct Code#>[CRLF]\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1110 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2110 |\n| 1 | Software Version | Variable | The HSM software version information. |\n| 2 | Image ID | Variable | The HSM image name, version number and creation date. |\n| 3 | Image CRC Checksum | 4 | The CRC checksum of the HSM software. |\n| 4 | Product Code | 1 | This field contains a decimal digit, 3 indicates AT1000. |\nUsage Note\nUse command <1100#> to obtain the extended HSM software version information.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1110#>\n```\n\nWhen the HSM is configured for the AKB personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:24:38#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-AKB | Version:   8.60, Date: |  | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:24:41#FC67#3#> |\nWhen the HSM is configured for the Variant personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:25:34#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-VAR | Version:   8.60, Date: |  | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:25:37#11C6#3#> |\nWhen the HSM is configured for the PCI-HSM personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:26:36#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-AKB | PCI-HSM   Version: | 8.60, | Date:   Jul   15 2024,   Time:   16:26:40#0551#3#> |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1110 - HSM System Configuration Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1110`\n- **Title:** HSM System Configuration Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1336 - 1336\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1336 -->\n\n1110 - HSM System Configuration Information\nCommand 1110 returns the HSM system software information, and cryptographic subsystem software\nversion information.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1110#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2110#Software Version Information#Image ID#Image CRC Checksum#\n```\n\nProduct Code#>[CRLF]\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1110 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2110 |\n| 1 | Software Version | Variable | The HSM software version information. |\n| 2 | Image ID | Variable | The HSM image name, version number and creation date. |\n| 3 | Image CRC Checksum | 4 | The CRC checksum of the HSM software. |\n| 4 | Product Code | 1 | This field contains a decimal digit, 3 indicates AT1000. |\nUsage Note\nUse command <1100#> to obtain the extended HSM software version information.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1110#>\n```\n\nWhen the HSM is configured for the AKB personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:24:38#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-AKB | Version:   8.60, Date: |  | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:24:41#FC67#3#> |\nWhen the HSM is configured for the Variant personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:25:34#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-VAR | Version:   8.60, Date: |  | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:25:37#11C6#3#> |\nWhen the HSM is configured for the PCI-HSM personality , it returns a response similar to this:\n| <2110#AT1000, | Version:   8.60, | Date: | Jul   15   2024,   Time:   16:26:36#Atalla   HSM |\n| AT1000-AKB | PCI-HSM   Version: | 8.60, | Date:   Jul   15 2024,   Time:   16:26:40#0551#3#> |\n\n"
