      "es": "# Command 1111 - HSM System Date and Time\n\n- **Command ID:** `1111`\n- **Title:** HSM System Date and Time\n- **PDF Pages:** 1337 - 1337\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1337 -->\n\n1111 - HSM System Date and Time\nCommand 1111 returns the HSM’s system date and time.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2111#YYMMDDHHMMSS#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1111 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2111 |\n| 1 | YYMMDDHHMMSS | 1 | The two digit year, two digit month, two digit day, two digit |\nhour, two digit minute, two digit second.\nUsage Notes\n By default, the time is Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). You can use the SCA HSM Time Adjustment\nfeature to specify a local time.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n| <2111#170525115300#> | (May 25, | 2017 | 11:53:00) |\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1111 - HSM System Date and Time\n\n- **Command ID:** `1111`\n- **Title:** HSM System Date and Time\n- **PDF Pages:** 1337 - 1337\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1337 -->\n\n1111 - HSM System Date and Time\nCommand 1111 returns the HSM’s system date and time.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2111#YYMMDDHHMMSS#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1111 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2111 |\n| 1 | YYMMDDHHMMSS | 1 | The two digit year, two digit month, two digit day, two digit |\nhour, two digit minute, two digit second.\nUsage Notes\n By default, the time is Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). You can use the SCA HSM Time Adjustment\nfeature to specify a local time.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1111#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n| <2111#170525115300#> | (May 25, | 2017 | 11:53:00) |\n\n"
