    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1200 - HSM Compliance Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1200`\n- **Title:** HSM Compliance Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1341 - 1342\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1341 -->\n\n1200 - HSM Compliance Information\nCommand 1200 returns the necessary information to confirm PCI-HSM or FIPS 140-3 compliance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2200#Certificate#Digital Signature#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1200 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2200 |\n| 1 | Personality Version | Variable | This line returns the HSM and Personality version along with |\nthe date the personality was implemented. This line is\nneeded for both PCI-HSM and FIPS140-3 validation.\nLoader Version Variable This line returns the Loader Version along with the\nimplementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3\nvalidation.\nPSMCU Version Variable This line returns the PSMCU version and the implementation\ndate. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation.\nCMS-OCT Version Variable This line returns the CMS-OCT version and the\nimplementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3\nvalidation.\n[CMS-NTX Version] Variable This line gives the CMS-NTX version and the implementation\ndate. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line\nwill not be present when the Nitrox chip is not present.\nChassis Version Variable This line returns the server chassis version. This line is\nneeded for PCI-HSM validation.\nACS Hardware Part Variable This line returns the ACS Hardware part number. This line is\nNumber needed for FIPS140-3 validation.\n\n\n<!-- Page 1342 -->\n\nUsage Note\n The response data consists of a single field, with individual version numbers separated into separate\nlines for human readability. These lines are described separately below.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\nWhen the HSM is configured with the AKB personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a response\nsimilar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\n| Atalla HSM | AT1000-AKB   Version: | 8.60.0.0, | Date: Jul   15   2024,   Time: 16:24:41 |\n| Loader Version | 1.22,   Nov | 20   2018 | 18:08:27 |\n| PSMCU Version | 1.0.0,   Nov | 4   2019 | 15:27:48 |\n| CMS-OCT | Version   1.0.0,   Oct 25 | 2019 | 13:08:19 |\n| CMS-NTX | Version   1.0.0,   Oct 25 | 2019 | 13:08:17 |\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the Variant personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a\nresponse similar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\nAtalla HSM AT1000-VAR Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:25:37\nLoader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27\nPSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov 4 2019 15:27:48\nCMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19\nCMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the PCI-HSM personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a\nresponse similar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\nAtalla HSM AT1000-AKB PCI-HSM Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:26:40\nLoader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27\nPSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov 4 2019 15:27:48\nCMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19\nCMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1200 - HSM Compliance Information\n\n- **Command ID:** `1200`\n- **Title:** HSM Compliance Information\n- **PDF Pages:** 1341 - 1342\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1341 -->\n\n1200 - HSM Compliance Information\nCommand 1200 returns the necessary information to confirm PCI-HSM or FIPS 140-3 compliance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2200#Certificate#Digital Signature#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1200 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2200 |\n| 1 | Personality Version | Variable | This line returns the HSM and Personality version along with |\nthe date the personality was implemented. This line is\nneeded for both PCI-HSM and FIPS140-3 validation.\nLoader Version Variable This line returns the Loader Version along with the\nimplementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3\nvalidation.\nPSMCU Version Variable This line returns the PSMCU version and the implementation\ndate. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation.\nCMS-OCT Version Variable This line returns the CMS-OCT version and the\nimplementation date. This line is needed for FIPS140-3\nvalidation.\n[CMS-NTX Version] Variable This line gives the CMS-NTX version and the implementation\ndate. This line is needed for FIPS140-3 validation. This line\nwill not be present when the Nitrox chip is not present.\nChassis Version Variable This line returns the server chassis version. This line is\nneeded for PCI-HSM validation.\nACS Hardware Part Variable This line returns the ACS Hardware part number. This line is\nNumber needed for FIPS140-3 validation.\n\n\n<!-- Page 1342 -->\n\nUsage Note\n The response data consists of a single field, with individual version numbers separated into separate\nlines for human readability. These lines are described separately below.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1200#>\n```\n\nWhen the HSM is configured with the AKB personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a response\nsimilar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\n| Atalla HSM | AT1000-AKB   Version: | 8.60.0.0, | Date: Jul   15   2024,   Time: 16:24:41 |\n| Loader Version | 1.22,   Nov | 20   2018 | 18:08:27 |\n| PSMCU Version | 1.0.0,   Nov | 4   2019 | 15:27:48 |\n| CMS-OCT | Version   1.0.0,   Oct 25 | 2019 | 13:08:19 |\n| CMS-NTX | Version   1.0.0,   Oct 25 | 2019 | 13:08:17 |\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the Variant personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a\nresponse similar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\nAtalla HSM AT1000-VAR Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:25:37\nLoader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27\nPSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov 4 2019 15:27:48\nCMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19\nCMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\nWhen the HSM is configured with the PCI-HSM personality and does not contain a Nitrox chip, it returns a\nresponse similar to this:\n\n```\n<2200#\n```\n\nAtalla HSM AT1000-AKB PCI-HSM Version: 8.60.0.0, Date: Jul 15 2024, Time: 16:26:40\nLoader Version 1.22, Nov 20 2018 18:08:27\nPSMCU Version 1.0.0, Nov 4 2019 15:27:48\nCMS-OCT Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:19\nCMS-NTX Version 1.0.0, Oct 25 2019 13:08:17\nHardware Chassis HW-AT-HSM-V1\nACS Adapter: C9B60-2108A\n#>\n\n"
    },
