      "es": "# Command 121 - Load RSA Key into RSA Key Table\n\n- **Command ID:** `121`\n- **Title:** Load RSA Key into RSA Key Table\n- **PDF Pages:** 731 - 732\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 731 -->\n\n121 - Load RSA Key into RSA Key Table\nCommand 121 stores either a public or private RSA key in the volatile RSA key table.\nReference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\nCommand\n| <121#Key | Slot#Public   Key | or   Private | Key#> |\nResponse\n\n```\n<221#Key Slot#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier   3 |  | 121 |\n| 1 | Key Slot   1 - 3 |  | The location in the RSA Key Table where the key will be |\nstored, erasing any existing value. This field contains a 1 - 3\ndecimal number in the range of 0 - 199. When this field\ncontains an asterisk character *, the private key will be stored\nin the first available empty key slot.\n| 2 | Public Key or Private Variable |  | The RSA-AKB of the public key or private key to be stored in |\nKey the RSA key table.\nThis field supports any valid RSA public or private key. To\ngenerate a current list of valid RSA headers, use command\n9A#HEADERS with a filter of ‘A.’\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII characters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier   2 |  | 221 |\n| 1 | Key Slot   3 |  | This field contains the location in the RSA Key Table where |\nthe key is stored. This field contains a 1 - 3 decimal number in\nthe range of 000 - 199.\n\n\n<!-- Page 732 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 2 | Check Digits   8 |  | The value of this field is based on the first digit of the header |\nof the key:\n1 = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters\nof the SHA-1 hash of the key.\n3 = field contains the leftmost eight hexadecimal characters\nof the SHA-256 hash of the public key.\nUsage Notes\n The value of the public exponent must be odd, cannot be 01, and must not exceed the value of the\nmodulus.\n When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 3key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the\nRSA key in AKBv1 format is 2048 bits. RSA keys under the AES MFK are unlimited.\n When the HSM is operating in PCI-HSM mode and contains a 2key-3DES MFK, the maximum size of the\nRSA key in AKBv1 format is 1024 bits. RSA keys under the AES MFK are unlimited.\nAKB 3DES MFK Example\nThe 3key-3DES Master File Key is:\n2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196. See “3key-3DES\nKey (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Key slot: 1\n Public Key:\n1SRVE000,00030100010100AF79E1E223A5DDC8EE7599D4817FDFAD04AAA3911D82D615C8F166E\n4C6391A9E5C8724628E62D9075836535642ABD14EAA681CD7EC8A42166870FB366E0863FC2C3A3\nB4969B9F46F1DA0C31D1B313B404ECC73AE15677D13FE086CE0758890FDF7455905948D4FD8276\n55FD96908EA4180611A2ED38D876CF31B23EC739F6F3F34048BFA3AEDA6090AFA205E1C19D0E32\n52366D3DC2C6BECBA6ABDDA79C899150302B3192F986AEF29674BA56A648A928A9ECB84DE2E46\n00D80538811AA7475CB6B559BA6D5D3C0D0F7F91A393B30266AAD1FB27DF6BDC7A938B64D96F9\n132501E5320CE0C93BD244C9B6A41172ABF9B9D927AB23313B17677293E9E15DB9ABB,F7929A1B2\n95C6A00\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<121#1#1SRVE000,00030100010100AF79E1E223A5DDC8EE7599D4817FDFAD04AAA3911D82D615\n```\n\nC8F166E4C6391A9E5C8724628E62D9075836535642ABD14EAA681CD7EC8A42166870FB366E0863\nFC2C3A3B4969B9F46F1DA0C31D1B313B404ECC73AE15677D13FE086CE0758890FDF7455905948D\n4FD827655FD96908EA4180611A2ED38D876CF31B23EC739F6F3F34048BFA3AEDA6090AFA205E1C\n19D0E3252366D3DC2C6BECBA6ABDDA79C899150302B3192F986AEF29674BA56A648A928A9ECB84\nDE2E4600D80538811AA7475CB6B559BA6D5D3C0D0F7F91A393B30266AAD1FB27DF6BDC7A938B64\nD96F9132501E5320CE0C93BD244C9B6A41172ABF9B9D927AB23313B17677293E9E15DB9ABB,F79\n29A1B295C6A00#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<221#001#8F6D7481#>\n```\n\n\n",
