      "es": "# Command 1216 - HSM Battery Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `1216`\n- **Title:** HSM Battery Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 1347 - 1348\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1347 -->\n\n1216 - HSM Battery Status\nCommand 1216 returns the status of the HSM batteries. The HSM includes non-rechargeable batteries that\npower the Atalla Cryptographic System’s physical security components only when the HSM is not\nconnected to an AC power source. The batteries are rated to last the life of the HSM, under normal\noperating conditions they do not require maintenance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2216#1#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the number 1. |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\n| 2 | Status | 4, 7, 8 | The battery status, where: |\nGOOD = the battery capacity is in the normal range.\nREPLACE = the batteries should be replaced, the HSM will\nnot zeroize if disconnected from AC power.\nCRITICAL = the batteries must be replaced immediately,\nthe HSM may zeroize if disconnected from AC\npower.\nEXPIRED = the HSM will zeroize if disconnected from AC\npower.\nUsage Note\nTo schedule a battery replacement, contact Atalla technical support or your local service representative.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 1348 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2216#1#GOOD#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1216 - HSM Battery Status\n\n- **Command ID:** `1216`\n- **Title:** HSM Battery Status\n- **PDF Pages:** 1347 - 1348\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1347 -->\n\n1216 - HSM Battery Status\nCommand 1216 returns the status of the HSM batteries. The HSM includes non-rechargeable batteries that\npower the Atalla Cryptographic System’s physical security components only when the HSM is not\nconnected to an AC power source. The batteries are rated to last the life of the HSM, under normal\noperating conditions they do not require maintenance.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2216#1#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the number 1. |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2216 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\n| 2 | Status | 4, 7, 8 | The battery status, where: |\nGOOD = the battery capacity is in the normal range.\nREPLACE = the batteries should be replaced, the HSM will\nnot zeroize if disconnected from AC power.\nCRITICAL = the batteries must be replaced immediately,\nthe HSM may zeroize if disconnected from AC\npower.\nEXPIRED = the HSM will zeroize if disconnected from AC\npower.\nUsage Note\nTo schedule a battery replacement, contact Atalla technical support or your local service representative.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1216#1#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 1348 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2216#1#GOOD#>\n```\n\n\n"
