      "es": "# Command 1221 - HSM IP Address\n\n- **Command ID:** `1221`\n- **Title:** HSM IP Address\n- **PDF Pages:** 1349 - 1349\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1349 -->\n\n1221 - HSM IP Address\nCommand 1221 returns the HSM’s active IPv4 addresses.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1221#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <2221#NIC1 | IP Address#[NIC2 | IP | Address#]>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1221 |\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2221 |\n| 1 | NIC1 IP address | 15 | This field contains the NIC1 IP address. |\n| 2 | [NIC2 IP address#] | [15] | This field is optional. It is present when the NIC2 IP address |\nis active.\nExample\nWhen only one NIC is active, the HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2221#127.0.0.1#>\n```\n\nWhen both NICs are active, the HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2221#127.0.0.1#127.0.1.2#>\n```\n\n\n",
