    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1222 - HSM Port Numbers\n\n- **Command ID:** `1222`\n- **Title:** HSM Port Numbers\n- **PDF Pages:** 1350 - 1351\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1350 -->\n\n1222 - HSM Port Numbers\nCommand 1222 returns the ports defined for a given domain. It can be sent to the ASCII, Management, and\nstatus ports. When used over the serial connection, the Domain field must be specified.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1222#[NIC]#[Domain]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <2222#Ports | List#[Ports | List   for second | NIC#]>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1222 |\n| 1 | [NIC] | 0, 1 | This field specifies the NIC to obtain the port numbers from. |\nPossible values are:\n1 = NIC1\n2 = NIC2\nB = Return ports for both NIC1 and NIC2\nIf this field is empty, ports for both NIC1 and NIC2 are\nreturned.\nLegal Characters: 1,2,B\n| 2 | [Domain] | 0, 1 | This field specifies the domain to obtain the port numbers |\nfrom.\nIf this field is empty, list the ports used by the current\ndomain. Otherwise, list the ports used by the indicated\ndomain.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2222 |\n| 1 | Ports List | Variable | The list of ports supported for the indicated NIC in the |\nformat of PORT NAME=Port Number, separated by\ncommas. The names of currently supported ports are ASCII,\nSTATUS, MANAGE, PRTCMD, REST, and PEMU. If a port is\nundefined, it will not be listed.\nLegal Characters: A-Z, 0-9\n\n\n<!-- Page 1351 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 2 | [Ports List for second | Variable | If field 1 of the command is B or empty, the list of ports |\nNIC#] supported for NIC2 in the same format as response field 1.\nLegal Characters: A-Z, 0-9\nUsage Note\n Utimaco is likely to add additional ports to the HSM in the future. If this happens, then the HSM may\nreturn more than the 6 port names currently defined. Utimaco recommends making the receiving\napplication flexible in the length and content of response fields.\nExample\nThe following definitions are present in the HSM’s config.prm file:\nPORT_ASCII = 7001\nPORT_ASCII_2 = 7011\nPORT_MANAGEMENT = 7101\nPORT_STATUS = 7201\nPORT_STATUS_2 = 7211\nPORT_REST = 8001\nThe following definitions are NOT present in the HSM’s config.prm file:\nPORT_PRTCMD, PORT_PEMU, PORT_MANAGEMENT_2, PORT_PEMU_2, PORT_REST_2\nGet all defined ports on both NICs\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1222###>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2222#ASCII=7001,MANAGE=7101,STATUS=7201,REST=8001#ASCII=7011,STATUS=7211#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1222 - HSM Port Numbers\n\n- **Command ID:** `1222`\n- **Title:** HSM Port Numbers\n- **PDF Pages:** 1350 - 1351\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1350 -->\n\n1222 - HSM Port Numbers\nCommand 1222 returns the ports defined for a given domain. It can be sent to the ASCII, Management, and\nstatus ports. When used over the serial connection, the Domain field must be specified.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1222#[NIC]#[Domain]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <2222#Ports | List#[Ports | List   for second | NIC#]>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1222 |\n| 1 | [NIC] | 0, 1 | This field specifies the NIC to obtain the port numbers from. |\nPossible values are:\n1 = NIC1\n2 = NIC2\nB = Return ports for both NIC1 and NIC2\nIf this field is empty, ports for both NIC1 and NIC2 are\nreturned.\nLegal Characters: 1,2,B\n| 2 | [Domain] | 0, 1 | This field specifies the domain to obtain the port numbers |\nfrom.\nIf this field is empty, list the ports used by the current\ndomain. Otherwise, list the ports used by the indicated\ndomain.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2222 |\n| 1 | Ports List | Variable | The list of ports supported for the indicated NIC in the |\nformat of PORT NAME=Port Number, separated by\ncommas. The names of currently supported ports are ASCII,\nSTATUS, MANAGE, PRTCMD, REST, and PEMU. If a port is\nundefined, it will not be listed.\nLegal Characters: A-Z, 0-9\n\n\n<!-- Page 1351 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 2 | [Ports List for second | Variable | If field 1 of the command is B or empty, the list of ports |\nNIC#] supported for NIC2 in the same format as response field 1.\nLegal Characters: A-Z, 0-9\nUsage Note\n Utimaco is likely to add additional ports to the HSM in the future. If this happens, then the HSM may\nreturn more than the 6 port names currently defined. Utimaco recommends making the receiving\napplication flexible in the length and content of response fields.\nExample\nThe following definitions are present in the HSM’s config.prm file:\nPORT_ASCII = 7001\nPORT_ASCII_2 = 7011\nPORT_MANAGEMENT = 7101\nPORT_STATUS = 7201\nPORT_STATUS_2 = 7211\nPORT_REST = 8001\nThe following definitions are NOT present in the HSM’s config.prm file:\nPORT_PRTCMD, PORT_PEMU, PORT_MANAGEMENT_2, PORT_PEMU_2, PORT_REST_2\nGet all defined ports on both NICs\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1222###>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2222#ASCII=7001,MANAGE=7101,STATUS=7201,REST=8001#ASCII=7011,STATUS=7211#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
