    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 1224 - HSM Remote Connections\n\n- **Command ID:** `1224`\n- **Title:** HSM Remote Connections\n- **PDF Pages:** 1354 - 1355\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1354 -->\n\n1224 - HSM Remote Connections\nCommand 1224 returns return the IP address of all remote computers connecting to the indicated NIC and\nport.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1224#[NIC]#[Port]#[Domain]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2224#IP Address List#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1224 |\n| 1 | [NIC] | 0, 1 | Indicates which NIC to query. Possible values are: |\n1 = NIC1\n2 = NIC2\nIf this field is empty, the current NIC is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 1,2\n| 2 | [Port] | 0, 4-5 | Indicates which Port to query. |\nIf this field is empty, the current Port is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 1024 - 65534\n| 3 | [Domain] | 0, 1 | Indicates which Domain to query. |\nIf this field is empty, the current Domain is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2224 |\n| 1 | IP Address List | Variable | Comma-separated list of IP addresses connected to the |\nindicated port in the format of IP Address = number of\nconnections.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, ',', '.', '='\n\n\n<!-- Page 1355 -->\n\nUsage Note\n This command returns a variable number of fields depending on the number of addresses attached to\nthe given port.\n This command does not support the PEMU and REST ports.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1224####>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2224#192.168.1.112=6,192.168.1.120=5#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1224 - HSM Remote Connections\n\n- **Command ID:** `1224`\n- **Title:** HSM Remote Connections\n- **PDF Pages:** 1354 - 1355\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1354 -->\n\n1224 - HSM Remote Connections\nCommand 1224 returns return the IP address of all remote computers connecting to the indicated NIC and\nport.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1224#[NIC]#[Port]#[Domain]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2224#IP Address List#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1224 |\n| 1 | [NIC] | 0, 1 | Indicates which NIC to query. Possible values are: |\n1 = NIC1\n2 = NIC2\nIf this field is empty, the current NIC is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 1,2\n| 2 | [Port] | 0, 4-5 | Indicates which Port to query. |\nIf this field is empty, the current Port is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 1024 - 65534\n| 3 | [Domain] | 0, 1 | Indicates which Domain to query. |\nIf this field is empty, the current Domain is assumed.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2224 |\n| 1 | IP Address List | Variable | Comma-separated list of IP addresses connected to the |\nindicated port in the format of IP Address = number of\nconnections.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, ',', '.', '='\n\n\n<!-- Page 1355 -->\n\nUsage Note\n This command returns a variable number of fields depending on the number of addresses attached to\nthe given port.\n This command does not support the PEMU and REST ports.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1224####>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns a response similar to this:\n\n```\n<2224#192.168.1.112=6,192.168.1.120=5#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
