      "es": "# Command 1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1228`\n- **Title:** Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1362 - 1362\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1362 -->\n\n1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\nCommand 1228 confirms the HSM’s reset to factory state. Prior to using this command, you must first use\ncommand 1227 to generate the input for field 1.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2228#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1228 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | n | This field contains the random challenge number returned |\nas field 1 of response to command 1227.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2228 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: |\nok = the HSM has been reset to factory state\nBad Confirmation = the wrong value was entered in\ncommand field 1, and the HSM has not been reset to factory\nstate. You must send command 1227 again to generate a\nnew challenge value, and then send command 1228 again.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2228#ok#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n\n- **Command ID:** `1228`\n- **Title:** Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\n- **PDF Pages:** 1362 - 1362\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1362 -->\n\n1228 - Confirm Reset HSM to Factory State\nCommand 1228 confirms the HSM’s reset to factory state. Prior to using this command, you must first use\ncommand 1227 to generate the input for field 1.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2228#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1228 |\n| 1 | nnnnnn | n | This field contains the random challenge number returned |\nas field 1 of response to command 1227.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2228 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: |\nok = the HSM has been reset to factory state\nBad Confirmation = the wrong value was entered in\ncommand field 1, and the HSM has not been reset to factory\nstate. You must send command 1227 again to generate a\nnew challenge value, and then send command 1228 again.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1228#nnnnnn#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2228#ok#>\n```\n\n\n"
