      "es": "# Command 1350 - Select HSM Domain\n\n- **Command ID:** `1350`\n- **Title:** Select HSM Domain\n- **PDF Pages:** 1366 - 1367\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1366 -->\n\n1350 - Select HSM Domain\nCommand 1350 selects which domain will process the commands sent from the serial port. The term\nVNSPx indicates the domain number. For example, to connect to Domain2, use VNSP2.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for\n> [!NOTE]\n> multiple Domains.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1350#VNSPx#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2350#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1350 |\n| 1 | VNSPx | 5 | The Domain number to process commands sent from the |\nserial port. For example, if commands from the serial port\nshould be processed by Domain2, the value in this file must\nbe VNSP2.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2350 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: |\nok = the Domain number specified in command field 1 will\nprocess commands sent to the serial port\nnot defined = the Domain number specified in command\nfield 1 is not defined in the config.prm file.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1350#VNSP3#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2350#ok#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 1367 -->\n\nIf the specified Domain has not been defined in the HSM’s config.prm file, the HSM returns the following\nresponse:\n\n```\n<2350#not defined#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 1350 - Select HSM Domain\n\n- **Command ID:** `1350`\n- **Title:** Select HSM Domain\n- **PDF Pages:** 1366 - 1367\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1366 -->\n\n1350 - Select HSM Domain\nCommand 1350 selects which domain will process the commands sent from the serial port. The term\nVNSPx indicates the domain number. For example, to connect to Domain2, use VNSP2.\n> [!NOTE]\n> NOTE: This command is only allowed on the serial port. It should only be sent to an HSM that is configured for\n> [!NOTE]\n> multiple Domains.\nCommand\n\n```\n<1350#VNSPx#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<2350#Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 4 | 1350 |\n| 1 | VNSPx | 5 | The Domain number to process commands sent from the |\nserial port. For example, if commands from the serial port\nshould be processed by Domain2, the value in this file must\nbe VNSP2.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 4 | 2350 |\n| 1 | Status | 2, 16 | This field contains the status result, where: |\nok = the Domain number specified in command field 1 will\nprocess commands sent to the serial port\nnot defined = the Domain number specified in command\nfield 1 is not defined in the config.prm file.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<1350#VNSP3#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<2350#ok#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 1367 -->\n\nIf the specified Domain has not been defined in the HSM’s config.prm file, the HSM returns the following\nresponse:\n\n```\n<2350#not defined#>\n```\n\n\n"
