      "es": "# Command 14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `14`\n- **Title:** Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 148 - 149\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 148 -->\n\n14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\nCommand 14 encrypts the ATM Master Key under an Encryption Key for downloading to Diebold ATMs.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<14#1#Variants#Master Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<24#1#Master Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 14 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variants | 2 | The MFK variants. This field contains two variant values. The |\nfirst variant value defines the type of Master Key which can\nbe downloaded to the ATM. The second variant value\ndefines the type of Encryption Key which is currently present\nin the ATM.\nThe following types of Mater Keys and their corresponding\nvariants can be downloaded.\nMAC Master Key = 1\nPIN Master Key = 5\nVisa Master Key = 5\nThe following types of Encryption Keys and their\ncorresponding variants can exist in the ATMs:\nCommunications Key = 1\nATMA Key = 5\nPIN Master Key-1 = 5\nVisa Master Key-1 = 5\n| 3 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under the proper variant of |\nthe MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal\ncharacters, or a volatile table location.\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The cryptogram of the key under which the ATM Master Key |\nis to be encrypted. This Encryption Key is encrypted under\nthe proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32\nhexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location.\n\n\n<!-- Page 149 -->\n\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 24 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The Master Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This |\nfield contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Master Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Master Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Manually load the ATM with its initial keys.\n Generate the appropriate Encryption Key for encrypting the ATM Master Key and encrypt it using the\nproper variant of the MFK. The Encryption Key length must be equal or greater than the length of the\nATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n Generate the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nLoad an ATM Master Key\n Variant: 1\n Variant: 5\n Clear-text Master Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\nThe Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:3219 92E9 44B0 F423 1DE1 CF68 9E96 99D6\n Clear-text Encryption Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Encryption Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C 608FC3DD BDDA\n3E56\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<14#1#15#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#118A17BA953BD16C608FC3DDBDDA3E56#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<24#1#CA652727D7ECC3FF29D072B935BEC86E#B15B#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `14`\n- **Title:** Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 148 - 149\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 148 -->\n\n14 - Load ATM Master Key, Diebold\nCommand 14 encrypts the ATM Master Key under an Encryption Key for downloading to Diebold ATMs.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<14#1#Variants#Master Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<24#1#Master Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 14 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variants | 2 | The MFK variants. This field contains two variant values. The |\nfirst variant value defines the type of Master Key which can\nbe downloaded to the ATM. The second variant value\ndefines the type of Encryption Key which is currently present\nin the ATM.\nThe following types of Mater Keys and their corresponding\nvariants can be downloaded.\nMAC Master Key = 1\nPIN Master Key = 5\nVisa Master Key = 5\nThe following types of Encryption Keys and their\ncorresponding variants can exist in the ATMs:\nCommunications Key = 1\nATMA Key = 5\nPIN Master Key-1 = 5\nVisa Master Key-1 = 5\n| 3 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under the proper variant of |\nthe MFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal\ncharacters, or a volatile table location.\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The cryptogram of the key under which the ATM Master Key |\nis to be encrypted. This Encryption Key is encrypted under\nthe proper variant of the MFK. This field contains 16 or 32\nhexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location.\n\n\n<!-- Page 149 -->\n\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 24 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Master Key | 16, 32 | The Master Key encrypted under the Encryption Key. This |\nfield contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Master Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Master Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Manually load the ATM with its initial keys.\n Generate the appropriate Encryption Key for encrypting the ATM Master Key and encrypt it using the\nproper variant of the MFK. The Encryption Key length must be equal or greater than the length of the\nATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\n Generate the ATM Master Key, it cannot be a replicated single-length key.\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nLoad an ATM Master Key\n Variant: 1\n Variant: 5\n Clear-text Master Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\nThe Master Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:3219 92E9 44B0 F423 1DE1 CF68 9E96 99D6\n Clear-text Encryption Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Encryption Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C 608FC3DD BDDA\n3E56\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<14#1#15#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#118A17BA953BD16C608FC3DDBDDA3E56#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<24#1#CA652727D7ECC3FF29D072B935BEC86E#B15B#>\n```\n\n\n"
