      "es": "# Command 143 - Import non-PTS Public Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `143`\n- **Title:** Import non-PTS Public Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 877 - 879\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 877 -->\n\n143 - Import non-PTS Public Key\nCommand 143 allows a MAC to be put on an RSA or ECC key that is used for non-PIN related activities.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION: There is no dual control over this command, so any user of the HSM can introduce a public key.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Keys loaded this way can never be used to encrypt PIN keys or key wrapping keys that can protect PIN keys,\n> [!CAUTION]\n> because PIN keys and the keys that protect them must always be under dual control.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<143#Header#Public Exponent/Curve#Modulus/Public Key x coordinate#\n```\n\n[Public key y coordinate]#>\nResponse\n\n```\n<243#Public Key#Check digits#>\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier   3 |  | 143 |\n| 1 | Header   8 |  | The AKB header to be applied to the public key. |\nHeaders Supported:\nRSA keys: 3KREN00N, 3sRVN000, 3pRVN000, 3DREN000.\nECDSA keys: 3seVN000, 3peVN000.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n| 2 | Public exponent Variable |  | RSA keys (AKB header byte 2 = R), the public key’s public |\nexponent. The value of the public exponent must be odd, it\nor cannot be 01 and it must be less than the value of the\nmodulus.\nCurve\nECC keys (AKB header byte 2 = e), the constant indicating\nthe named curve.\nSupported Values:\nCurve Constant\nNIST P-521 2B81040023\nNIST P-256 2A8648CE3D030107\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n\n<!-- Page 878 -->\n\n\n### Command description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 3 | RSA Modulus Variable |  | RSA keys, the public key’s modulus. If this value starts with |\n00, the 00 is not included in the AKB. The maximum size of\nor the RSA modulus is 4096 bits (ignoring leading zeros). The\nminimum size is 1024 bits. This command ignores option\n8F.\nECC public key x\ncoordinate ECC keys, the x coordinate of the public key (Qx).\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n| 4 | [Public key y Variable |  | RSA keys, this field must be empty. |\ncoordinate]\nECC keys, the y coordinate of the public key (Qy).\nEMV EC-SDSA keys, this field may be empty.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n0 Response identifier 3 243\n| 1 | Public Key   Variable |  | The public key, in AKB format, version 3. |\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n2 Check digits 8 The first 8 digits from the SHA-256 hash of the public key.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nAKB AES MFK Examples\nAES Master File Key = 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF\nFEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62, see “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component\nvalues.\nRSA Example\n The clear value of the RSA Public Key is:\n e = 0x10001\n n =\n949ABD9347386F167B627276DCF86DEE354700DFCBD8B2BA1D6B0014E5267573B880480A656\n47EAC78C633FD27B6A6206D983B65847EBF3EFB6074B608D7474261C9EE69341D97764A4875F\nD8859E670D953577427D83956C0A824B2E2A5EF65F00E602AC1250C4E7994B393DA7C210D5E\n23EA983606731DE7F28E3736CFB663\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<143#3KREN00N#010001#949ABD9347386F167B627276DCF86DEE354700DFCBD8B2BA1D6B0014E\n```\n\n5267573B880480A65647EAC78C633FD27B6A6206D983B65847EBF3EFB6074B608D7474261C9EE6\n9341D97764A4875FD8859E670D953577427D83956C0A824B2E2A5EF65F00E602AC1250C4E7994B\n393DA7C210D5E23EA983606731DE7F28E3736CFB663##>\n\n\n<!-- Page 879 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<243#3KREN00N,00030100010080949ABD9347386F167B627276DCF86DEE354700DFCBD8B2BA1D\n```\n\n6B0014E5267573B880480A65647EAC78C633FD27B6A6206D983B65847EBF3EFB6074B608D74742\n61C9EE69341D97764A4875FD8859E670D953577427D83956C0A824B2E2A5EF65F00E602AC1250C\n4E7994B393DA7C210D5E23EA983606731DE7F28E3736CFB663,5E8ECA06604C6B4E787A5F583C3\n6E654#168D48E8#>\nECDSA Example\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<143#3seVN000#2A8648CE3D030107#DFA1F8B073A022BB5620E6F1BD78A5C778309587D87754C\n```\n\nA8DDBFC89D4258652#2A7C063F2AF9EACEA3BE2DB7A8C44CCCC0693A732D9E6818365C7997C698\nCEDD#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<243#3seVN000,00082A8648CE3D0301070020DFA1F8B073A022BB5620E6F1BD78A5C778309587\n```\n\nD87754CA8DDBFC89D425865200202A7C063F2AF9EACEA3BE2DB7A8C44CCCC0693A732D9E681836\n5C7997C698CEDD,E14C5DDC96CEEAFC4C1F489B7F55699C#F5849197#>\n\n",
