    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `15`\n- **Title:** Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 158 - 159\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 158 -->\n\n15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\nCommand 15 encrypts a Communications Key for downloading to a Diebold ATM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<15#1#Variant#Communications Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <25#1#Communications | Key#Check |  | Digits#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 15 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The MFK variant under which the Encryption Key was |\nencrypted. This field contains a number, either 1 or 5.\n| 3 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the |\nMFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters,\nor a volatile table location.\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The Encryption Key encrypted under the variant 1 or 5 of the |\nMFK. This key encrypts the Communications Key. If the\nvariant specified in field 2 is 1, the old Communications Key\nencrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. If the\nvariant specified in field 2 is 5, the PIN Master Key encrypts\nthe Communications Key supplied in field 3.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 25 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under the Encryption |\nKey. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Communications Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Communications Key. If option 88 is enabled, the\nleftmost six check digits are returned.\n\n\n<!-- Page 159 -->\n\nUsage Notes\n The Communications Key in a Diebold ATM encrypts PINs; therefore, although the term\ncommunications key is used for this key, it is supported in the Atalla key management scheme as a PIN\nEncryption Key.\n Generate the Encryption Key which will encrypt the new Communications Key.\n Generate the new Communications Key (KC).\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Variant: 1\n Clear-text new Communications Key: 0123456789ABCDEF 1111222233334444\nThe new Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86D417E64E07E0\nD538A881DE91EAF1\n Clear-text Encryption Key (P):3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\nThe Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 321992E944B0F423 1DE1CF689E9699D6\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<15#1#1#AE86D417E64E07E0D538A881DE91EAF1#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<25#1#4DEB22EE1652AA8A216FF8BA794E8AFD#4E15#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `15`\n- **Title:** Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 158 - 159\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 158 -->\n\n15 - Change ATM Communications Key, Diebold\nCommand 15 encrypts a Communications Key for downloading to a Diebold ATM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<15#1#Variant#Communications Key#Encryption Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n| <25#1#Communications | Key#Check |  | Digits#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 15 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The MFK variant under which the Encryption Key was |\nencrypted. This field contains a number, either 1 or 5.\n| 3 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the |\nMFK. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters,\nor a volatile table location.\n| 4 | Encryption Key | 16, 32 | The Encryption Key encrypted under the variant 1 or 5 of the |\nMFK. This key encrypts the Communications Key. If the\nvariant specified in field 2 is 1, the old Communications Key\nencrypts the Communications Key supplied in field 3. If the\nvariant specified in field 2 is 5, the PIN Master Key encrypts\nthe Communications Key supplied in field 3.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 25 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16, 32 | The Communications Key encrypted under the Encryption |\nKey. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Communications Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Communications Key. If option 88 is enabled, the\nleftmost six check digits are returned.\n\n\n<!-- Page 159 -->\n\nUsage Notes\n The Communications Key in a Diebold ATM encrypts PINs; therefore, although the term\ncommunications key is used for this key, it is supported in the Atalla key management scheme as a PIN\nEncryption Key.\n Generate the Encryption Key which will encrypt the new Communications Key.\n Generate the new Communications Key (KC).\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Variant: 1\n Clear-text new Communications Key: 0123456789ABCDEF 1111222233334444\nThe new Communications Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86D417E64E07E0\nD538A881DE91EAF1\n Clear-text Encryption Key (P):3333 3333 3333 3333 5555 6666 7777 8888\nThe Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: 321992E944B0F423 1DE1CF689E9699D6\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<15#1#1#AE86D417E64E07E0D538A881DE91EAF1#321992E944B0F4231DE1CF689E9699D6#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<25#1#4DEB22EE1652AA8A216FF8BA794E8AFD#4E15#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
