      "es": "# Command 15 - Change ATM Communications Key, IBM 4731\n\n- **Command ID:** `15`\n- **Title:** Change ATM Communications Key, IBM 4731\n- **PDF Pages:** 167 - 169\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 167 -->\n\n15 - Change ATM Communications Key, IBM 4731\nCommand 15 generates a random Communication Key for downloading to an IBM 4731 ATM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<15#4#Exchange Key#Message#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<25#4#Communications Key#Communications Key#Message#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 15 |\n| 1 | 4 | 1 | 4 = IBM 4731 |\n| 2 | Exchange Key | 74 | The Exchange Key encrypted under the MFK. This field |\ncontains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\nHeaders Supported: 3DES MFK\n1KDN*000, 1KDE*000, where * = E or N.\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3KDN*000, 3KDE*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n16 The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 3 of the MFK.\nThis field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\n| 3 | Message | 8 | The IBM 4731 message. This field contains 8 hexadecimal |\ncharacters.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 25 |\n| 1 | 4 | 1 | 4 = IBM 4731 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 168 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 74 | The Communications Key encrypted under the MFK. This |\nfield contains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\nHeaders Supported: 1KDNE000 and 1KDEE000.\n16 The Communications Key encrypted under variant 3 of the\nMFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a\nvolatile table location.\n| 3 | Communications Key | 16 | The Communications Key encrypted under the Exchange |\nKey. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 4 | Message | 16 | The IBM 4731 message encrypted under the |\nCommunications Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal\ncharacters.\n| 5 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Communications Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Communications Key. If option 88 is enabled, the\nleftmost six check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\nAKB usage notes Variant usage notes\n\n### Usage Notes\n\n| 🟧 AKB Usage Notes | 🟪 Variant Usage Notes |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| This command supports 1key-3DES (single-length)<br>keys only if 6C is enabled. | All keys must be 1key-3DES keys. |\n\nAKB 3DES MFK Example\nThe 3key-3DES Master File Key is:\n2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196.\nSee “3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nThis command generates data which is returned in the response, your responses will not exactly match the\nresponses shown below.\n Clear-text Exchange Key (KX): 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Exchange Key in AKB format:\n1KDNE000,7BC98D21224A2C853A3C48A2A09AF7905CDD901CD903FAE1,FBBDF27401D4CCD8\n Message: 01234567\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<15#4#1KDNE000,7BC98D21224A2C853A3C48A2A09AF7905CDD901CD903FAE1,FBBDF27401D4CC\n```\n\nD8#01234567#>\nThe HSM returns a similar response:\n\n```\n<25#4#1c7NE000,CDBDE2F596449C8D0E909218BCBEC47757F5D11508334E2F,985E755F059CB5\n```\n\n4E#C9E13778E0AADFB6#ECFC979E884DC6F5#1D8F#>\n\n\n<!-- Page 169 -->\n\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF\nFEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component\nvalues.\nThis command generates data which is returned in the response, your responses will not exactly match the\nresponses shown below.\n Clear-text Exchange Key (KX): 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Exchange Key in AKB format:\n3KDNE000,D46AD0EF3362928E263A7E3439FF28B7DFB5B97F7CAFD2F0,B0D8A90A81883B40\n Message: 01234567\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<15#4#3KDNE000,D46AD0EF3362928E263A7E3439FF28B7DFB5B97F7CAFD2F0,B0D8A90A81883B\n```\n\n40#01234567#>\nThe HSM returns a similar response:\n\n```\n<25#4#1c7NE000,646FA3E8D4FA6374122374823BAE4E7F40358FD50B314C9F,CCBC2C3F76FA93\n```\n\n09#8D5F85E734874448#5AC079405456F8E0#9EB5#>\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nThis command generates data which is returned in the response, your responses will not exactly match the\nresponses shown below.\n Clear-text Exchange Key (KX): 0123 4567 89AB CDEF 1111 2222 3333 4444\nThe Exchange Key (KX) encrypted under variant 0 of the MFK: 9007 B875 1BB7 AB4E 45ED 2536 2B16\n0750\n Message: 01234567\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<15#4#9007B8751BB7AB4E45ED25362B160750#01234567#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns a similar response:\n\n```\n<25#4#9986C1DB8ABE561D#CE7A35D9A2787D86#60EF4DE29208C532#E6C0#>\n```\n\n\n",
