      "es": "# Command 155 - Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using EC-SDSA\n\n- **Command ID:** `155`\n- **Title:** Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using EC-SDSA\n- **PDF Pages:** 932 - 933\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 932 -->\n\n155 - Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using\nEC-SDSA\nCommand 155 verifies an ISO/IEC 14888-3 digital signature as needed to support EMV using the Elliptic\nCurve Schnorr's Digital Signature Algorithm (EC-SDSA).\nReference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<155#Signature Algorithm#MSG#Digital Signature#Public Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<155#Verification Flag#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier   3 |  | 155 |\n| 1 | Signature Algorithm   2 |  | The algorithm used to generate the message digest. |\n10 = EC-SDSA with SHA-256 using curve P-256\n11 = EC-SDSA with SHA-512 using curve P-521\nLegal Characters: 10, 11\n| 2 | MSG   2 - 4096 |  | Input data to verify the signature. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n| 3 | Digital Signature   128, 260 |  | The digital signature to be verified. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n| 4 | Public Key   Variable |  | The Public Key to verify the digital signature. |\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3peV*000, where * = E, N, or S.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier   3 |  | 255 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 933 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 1 | Verification Flag   1 |  | The indicator of whether the digital signature was verified. |\nY = yes, signature verified\nN = no, signature did not verify\nLegal Characters: Y, N\n| 2 | Check Digits   8 |  | The Public Key check digits are the leftmost eight |\nhexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash result of the\nPublic Key.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is:\n2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\ncheck digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Private Key: A5483159423A754D46DC4ED22997686D8BA79AB978AB3FD42BA441B3AC58F9DF\n Message:\n15\n0000000002990000000000000056000000000009782304010011223344220100029F2701409F360\n200029F260839656889ABC1AFFC9F10200FA5019A3800000000000000000000000F01000000000\n0000000000000000000\n Public key point: 04||x||y\n04F0D3853D5417FDB5D4204193026B25935DB66A64B255C711F03E5C32FFC7894E\n6C180EE3B9D5453F70033F2C252B6E1A211FF072EDFC289093D51D6856C5CBA2\n The XDA signature is S =\n(10DD8EC1D542F5362485EBF8EF71B99512CBE7361A3D453431CF5F64F58CA9B0,\nFDCC65D7F032BE0939C9F3C0B246C00904A0CE25053512153140FE4E78801523)\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<155#10#150000000002990000000000000056000000000009782304010011223344220100029F\n```\n\n2701409F360200029F260839656889ABC1AFFC9F10200FA5019A3800000000000000000000000F\n010000000000000000000000000000#10DD8EC1D542F5362485EBF8EF71B99512CBE7361A3D453\n431CF5F64F58CA9B0FDCC65D7F032BE0939C9F3C0B246C00904A0CE25053512153140FE4E78801\n523#3peVE000,00082A8648CE3D0301070020F0D3853D5417FDB5D4204193026B25935DB66A64B\n255C711F03E5C32FFC7894E00206C180EE3B9D5453F70033F2C252B6E1A211FF072EDFC289093D\n51D6856C5CBA2,8838BFB07C720A9568EA8EA76EA7BFE1#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<255#Y#3FC92FAD#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 155 - Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using EC-SDSA\n\n- **Command ID:** `155`\n- **Title:** Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using EC-SDSA\n- **PDF Pages:** 932 - 933\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 932 -->\n\n155 - Verify ISO/IEC 14888-3 Digital Signature using\nEC-SDSA\nCommand 155 verifies an ISO/IEC 14888-3 digital signature as needed to support EMV using the Elliptic\nCurve Schnorr's Digital Signature Algorithm (EC-SDSA).\nReference Information: Section 9, “Asymmetric Cryptography.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<155#Signature Algorithm#MSG#Digital Signature#Public Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<155#Verification Flag#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier   3 |  | 155 |\n| 1 | Signature Algorithm   2 |  | The algorithm used to generate the message digest. |\n10 = EC-SDSA with SHA-256 using curve P-256\n11 = EC-SDSA with SHA-512 using curve P-521\nLegal Characters: 10, 11\n| 2 | MSG   2 - 4096 |  | Input data to verify the signature. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n| 3 | Digital Signature   128, 260 |  | The digital signature to be verified. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n| 4 | Public Key   Variable |  | The Public Key to verify the digital signature. |\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3peV*000, where * = E, N, or S.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier   3 |  | 255 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 933 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents   Length |  | Description |\n| 1 | Verification Flag   1 |  | The indicator of whether the digital signature was verified. |\nY = yes, signature verified\nN = no, signature did not verify\nLegal Characters: Y, N\n| 2 | Check Digits   8 |  | The Public Key check digits are the leftmost eight |\nhexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 hash result of the\nPublic Key.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is:\n2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\ncheck digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Private Key: A5483159423A754D46DC4ED22997686D8BA79AB978AB3FD42BA441B3AC58F9DF\n Message:\n15\n0000000002990000000000000056000000000009782304010011223344220100029F2701409F360\n200029F260839656889ABC1AFFC9F10200FA5019A3800000000000000000000000F01000000000\n0000000000000000000\n Public key point: 04||x||y\n04F0D3853D5417FDB5D4204193026B25935DB66A64B255C711F03E5C32FFC7894E\n6C180EE3B9D5453F70033F2C252B6E1A211FF072EDFC289093D51D6856C5CBA2\n The XDA signature is S =\n(10DD8EC1D542F5362485EBF8EF71B99512CBE7361A3D453431CF5F64F58CA9B0,\nFDCC65D7F032BE0939C9F3C0B246C00904A0CE25053512153140FE4E78801523)\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<155#10#150000000002990000000000000056000000000009782304010011223344220100029F\n```\n\n2701409F360200029F260839656889ABC1AFFC9F10200FA5019A3800000000000000000000000F\n010000000000000000000000000000#10DD8EC1D542F5362485EBF8EF71B99512CBE7361A3D453\n431CF5F64F58CA9B0FDCC65D7F032BE0939C9F3C0B246C00904A0CE25053512153140FE4E78801\n523#3peVE000,00082A8648CE3D0301070020F0D3853D5417FDB5D4204193026B25935DB66A64B\n255C711F03E5C32FFC7894E00206C180EE3B9D5453F70033F2C252B6E1A211FF072EDFC289093D\n51D6856C5CBA2,8838BFB07C720A9568EA8EA76EA7BFE1#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<255#Y#3FC92FAD#>\n```\n\n\n"
