      "es": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 170 - 171\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 170 -->\n\n16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\nCommand 16 encrypts a Working Key to be downloaded to a Diebold ATM Financial Institution Table.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<16#1#Variant#Working Key#Exchange Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<26#1#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The variant to be applied to the MFK when encrypting the |\nWorking Key. This field contains a decimal number, either 2\nor 5.\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 or 5 of the MFK. |\nThis field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\n| 4 | Exchange Key | 16 | The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. |\nThis key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16\nhexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Exchange Key. This |\nfield contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Each execution of this command encrypts a single key for a FIT entry.\n\n\n<!-- Page 171 -->\n\n Generate the Exchange Key.\n All keys must be 1key-3DES keys.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text Working Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333\nThe Working Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: C22F 5A1F 22D1 ABF1\n Clear-text Exchange Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111\nThe Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<16#1#2#C22F5A1F22D1ABF1#118A17BA953BD16C#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<26#1#F679786E2411E3DE#ADC6#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\n- **PDF Pages:** 170 - 171\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 170 -->\n\n16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Diebold\nCommand 16 encrypts a Working Key to be downloaded to a Diebold ATM Financial Institution Table.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<16#1#Variant#Working Key#Exchange Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<26#1#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Variant | 1 | The variant to be applied to the MFK when encrypting the |\nWorking Key. This field contains a decimal number, either 2\nor 5.\n| 3 | Working Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under variant 2 or 5 of the MFK. |\nThis field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\n| 4 | Exchange Key | 16 | The Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. |\nThis key encrypts the Working Key. This field contains 16\nhexadecimal characters, or a volatile table location.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 = Diebold |\n| 2 | Communications Key | 16 | The Working Key encrypted under the Exchange Key. This |\nfield contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Each execution of this command encrypts a single key for a FIT entry.\n\n\n<!-- Page 171 -->\n\n Generate the Exchange Key.\n All keys must be 1key-3DES keys.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text Working Key: 3333 3333 3333 3333\nThe Working Key encrypted under variant 2 of the MFK: C22F 5A1F 22D1 ABF1\n Clear-text Exchange Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111\nThe Exchange Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK:118A 17BA 953B D16C\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<16#1#2#C22F5A1F22D1ABF1#118A17BA953BD16C#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<26#1#F679786E2411E3DE#ADC6#>\n```\n\n\n"
