      "es": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\n- **PDF Pages:** 172 - 173\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 172 -->\n\n16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\nCommand 16 encrypts a PIN Verification Key to be downloaded to a Docutel ATM Financial Institution\nTable.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n| <16#2#PIN | Verification   Key#ATM |  | Master   Key#> |\nResponse\n\n```\n<26#2#PIN Verification Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 = Docutel |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the |\nMFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a\nvolatile table location.\n| 3 | ATM Master Key | 16 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. |\nThis key encrypts the PIN Verification Key. This field\ncontains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 = Docutel |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under the ATM Master |\nKey. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The PIN Verification Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the PIN Verification Key. If option 88 is enabled, the\nleftmost six check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Generate the PIN Verification Key.\n\n\n<!-- Page 173 -->\n\n Generate the ATM Master Key.\n All keys must be 1key-3DES keys.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text PIN Verification Key: 2222 2222 2222 2222\nThe PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: EA45 F59C 6242 F687\n Clear-text ATM Master Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111\nThe ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: 118A 17BA 953B D16C\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<16#2#EA45F59C6242F687#118A17BA953BD16C#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<26#2#950973182317F80B#0096#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\n\n- **Command ID:** `16`\n- **Title:** Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\n- **PDF Pages:** 172 - 173\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 172 -->\n\n16 - Encrypt Financial Institution Table, Docutel\nCommand 16 encrypts a PIN Verification Key to be downloaded to a Docutel ATM Financial Institution\nTable.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n| <16#2#PIN | Verification   Key#ATM |  | Master   Key#> |\nResponse\n\n```\n<26#2#PIN Verification Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 16 |\n| 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 = Docutel |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the |\nMFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a\nvolatile table location.\n| 3 | ATM Master Key | 16 | The ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK. |\nThis key encrypts the PIN Verification Key. This field\ncontains 16 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 26 |\n| 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 = Docutel |\n| 2 | PIN Verification Key | 16 | The PIN Verification Key encrypted under the ATM Master |\nKey. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The PIN Verification Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the PIN Verification Key. If option 88 is enabled, the\nleftmost six check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Generate the PIN Verification Key.\n\n\n<!-- Page 173 -->\n\n Generate the ATM Master Key.\n All keys must be 1key-3DES keys.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text PIN Verification Key: 2222 2222 2222 2222\nThe PIN Verification Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: EA45 F59C 6242 F687\n Clear-text ATM Master Key: 1111 1111 1111 1111\nThe ATM Master Key encrypted under variant 5 of the MFK: 118A 17BA 953B D16C\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<16#2#EA45F59C6242F687#118A17BA953BD16C#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<26#2#950973182317F80B#0096#>\n```\n\n\n"
