      "es": "# Command 179 - Generate EMV AES MAC\n\n- **Command ID:** `179`\n- **Title:** Generate EMV AES MAC\n- **PDF Pages:** 1005 - 1008\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 1005 -->\n\n179 - Generate EMV AES MAC\nCommand 179 supports EMV issuer scripting. It generates a Message Authentication Code in accordance\nwith EMV standards using AES-based derivation.\nReference Information: Section 7, “Processing EMV and Visa stored value cards.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled AES\nCommand\n| <179#EMV | Derivation   Type#Issuer |  | Master   Key   -   MAC#Application   PAN# |\n| [Application PAN | Sequence | Number]#Diversification | Data#MAC   Length# |\n[Continuation IV]#Padded Data#>\nResponse\n\n```\n<279#MAC Length#MAC or Continuation IV#Session Key Check Digits#\n```\n\nIssuer Master Key - MAC Check Digits#>\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 3 | 179 |\n| 1 | Derivation Type | 1 | This field determines what keys are used to generate the |\nMAC and how they are derived. The following derivation\ntype is supported:\nA = Method C and EMV common session from the EMV\nv4.3 Book 2. A session key of the same length as the Issuer\nMaster Key is produced.\nLegal Characters: A\n| 2 | Issuer Master Key - MAC | 74, 90, | The Issuer Master Key for Message Integrity. This key must |\n106, be an AES 128, 192, or 256 bit key.\n110\nHeaders Supported: 3mJN*00M, where * = E, S, or N.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n| 3 | Application PAN | 1-20 | The Primary Account Number (PAN). |\nLegal Characters: 0 - 9\n| 4 | [Application PAN | 0, 2 | The optional application PAN Sequence Number. This field |\nSequence Number] may contain a 2-digit decimal value. If this field is empty,\nthe HSM will use a PAN Sequence Number of 00.\nLegal Characters: 0 - 9\n| 5 | Diversification Data | 16 | This field contains the Application Cryptogram. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n\n<!-- Page 1006 -->\n\n\n### Command description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 6 | MAC Length | 1 | The size of the MAC to be generated. Allowed values are: |\n0 = More data expected, no MAC verified.\n1 = 64 bits\nLegal Characters: 0-1\n| 7 | [Continuation IV] | 0, 74, | There are two use cases when this field must be empty: |\n110\n- When all of the data to be MACed is supplied in field 8.\n- When field 8 contains the first portion of the data to be\nMACed. The header for the continuation IV in response\nfield 2 will be 1IJNE00c.\nIf the MAC calculation is continued from a previous\ncommand, this field should contain the continuation-IV\nfrom response field 2.\nHeaders Supported: 3IJN*00c, where * = E, N, or S.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n| 8 | Padded Data | 16 - | The data used to calculate the MAC. Per the EMV |\n3584 specification, the data should be right-padded with a single\nbyte (expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"80\"),\nfollowed by a variable number of binary zeros bytes\n(expressed as two hexadecimal characters \"00\") to make\nthe total data length a multiple of 16 bytes (32 hexadecimal\ncharacters).\nThe HSM does not enforce this data format; it only requires\nthat the length of data is a multiple of 32 hexadecimal\ncharacters.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 3 | 278 |\n| 1 | MAC Length | 1 | This field contains the value of command field 6. |\nLegal Characters: 0, 1\n| 2 | MAC | 16 | This field will contain the calculated MAC. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nor\nContinuation IV 74, 110 If command field 6 is 0, then this field contains the\ncontinuation IV encrypted under the AES MFK using header\nsupplied in command field 7.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n| 3 | Session Key check digits | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. |\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\n\n\n<!-- Page 1007 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 4 | Issuer Master Key - MAC | 10 | The leftmost 10 digits of the CMAC of all zeros. |\ncheck digits\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nAKB AES MFK Examples\nThe AES Master File Key is:\n2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF FEDCBA9876543210\ncheck digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component values.\nAES 128-bit derived keys\n Derivation Type = A\n Cleartext Issuer Master Key: 01234567 88AACCEE FEDCBA98 77553311, check digits B6C18C1768\nThe Issuer Master Key in AKB format:\n3mJNE00M,4DB8E327B725A0D6704A392B701FF58B75B9F6DAD44DF951A896424512382E506812,\n6F8D65789174362AB38AB68DD6D3F013\n PAN = 01234567890123\n PSN = 45\n Diversification Data = 98765432 10987654\n Padded Data = 0011223344556677889900112233445580000000000000000000000000000000\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<179#A#3mJNE00M,4DB8E327B725A0D6704A392B701FF58B75B9F6DAD44DF951A896424512382E\n```\n\n506812,6F8D65789174362AB38AB68DD6D3F013#01234567890123#45#9876543210987654#1##\n0011223344556677889900112233445580000000000000000000000000000000#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<279#1#4884E9987A33D3F7#47978C93CB# B6C18C1768#>\n```\n\nAES 128-bit derived keys with continuation\n Derivation data = A\n Cleartext Issuer Master Key: 01234567 88AACCEE FEDCBA98 77553311, check digits B6C18C1768\nThe Issuer Master Key in AKB format:\n3mJNE00M,4DB8E327B725A0D6704A392B701FF58B75B9F6DAD44DF951A896424512382E506812,\n6F8D65789174362AB38AB68DD6D3F013\n PAN = 01234567890123\n PSN = 45\n Diversification Data = 98765432 10987654\n Padded Data = 0011223344556677889900112233445580000000000000000000000000000000\n\n\n<!-- Page 1008 -->\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<179#A#3mJNE00M,73C8EF1221849A7667CFBEBA725B976C,2EA2F9CE0C1987785F7D6F605D01D\n```\n\n08A#01234567890123#45#9876543210987654#0##00112233445566778899001122334455#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<279#0#3IJNE00c,F24D13E23760D62DC8642927C2CD6ED7,E604F28DB874B49C97824750513D0\n```\n\n747#47978C93CB#B6C18C1768#>\nThe command 2 looks like this:\n\n```\n<179#A#3mJNE00M,73C8EF1221849A7667CFBEBA725B976C,2EA2F9CE0C1987785F7D6F605D01D\n```\n\n08A#01234567890123#45#9876543210987654#1#3IJNE00c,F24D13E23760D62DC8642927C2CD\n6ED7,E604F28DB874B49C97824750513D0747#80000000000000000000000000000000#>\nThe response 2 looks like this:\n\n```\n<279#1#4884E9987A33D3F7#47978C93CB#B6C18C1768#>\n```\n\nAES 256-bit derived keys\n Derivation Type = A\n Cleartext Issuer Master Key: F1F1F1F1 F0F0F0F0 F2F2F2F2 F3F3F3F3 F4F4F4F4 F5F5F5F5\nF8F8F8F8 F9F9F9F9, check digits 01DBF370BC\nThe Issuer Master Key in AKB format:\n3mJNE00a,E8E7C6329E0172AF9E2F72B6A0735B986E95BB788D542EDF113AC7CB6A87FAFBAD37,\n6FAD04F505696D2DBA08DE293009554F\n PAN = 01234567890123\n PSN = 45\n Diversification Data = 98765432 10987654\n Padded Data = 0011223344556677889900112233445580000000000000000000000000000000\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<179#A#3mJNE00M,45CC35CE1868CDE33F6C895C67FB3982A5DC271DAB70251DC23C264E167CAB\n```\n\n09AE4F,80F6E549BFA7E41D94953AD30F2F4EB4#01234567890123#45#9876543210987654#1##\n0011223344556677889900112233445580000000000000000000000000000000#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<279#1#A41355E61FE934DF#457AFEBA71#01DBF370BC#>\n```\n\n\n",
