      "es": "# Command 18 - Generate Visa Working Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `18`\n- **Title:** Generate Visa Working Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 176 - 177\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 176 -->\n\n18 - Generate Visa Working Key\nCommand 18 generates a 1key-3DES Visa Working Key. This command uses the HSM’s Deterministic\nRandom Bit Generator (DRBG) to generate an odd-parity key.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<18#Key Exchange Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<28#Visa Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 18 |\n| 1 | Key Exchange Key | 16, 32 | The KEK encrypted under variant zero of the MFK. This key |\nencrypts the randomly generated Visa Working Key. Visa\nrefers to the KEK as a Zone Control Master Key (ZCMK). This\nfield can contain 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a\nvolatile table location.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 28 |\n| 1 | Visa Working Key | 16 | The Visa Working Key encrypted under the Key Exchange |\nKey. The host application sends this cryptogram to the\nremote node. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 2 | Visa Working Key | 16 | The Visa Working Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK |\nspecified in field 1 of the command. The host application\nstores this cryptogram on its key database for subsequent\nuse. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 6 | The Visa Working Key check digits are the leftmost six |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Visa Working Key.\nUsage Notes\n Generate the KEK.\n\n\n<!-- Page 177 -->\n\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES\nKey (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nThis command generates a random value, your results will be different.\n Clear-text Key Exchange Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Key Exchange Key encrypted under variant 0 of the MFK: 9007 B875 1BB7 AB4E\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<18#9007B8751BB7AB4E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<28#EA3310FF19DB4F4C#6CE476EF7B6E4776#7DE170#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 18 - Generate Visa Working Key\n\n- **Command ID:** `18`\n- **Title:** Generate Visa Working Key\n- **PDF Pages:** 176 - 177\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 176 -->\n\n18 - Generate Visa Working Key\nCommand 18 generates a 1key-3DES Visa Working Key. This command uses the HSM’s Deterministic\nRandom Bit Generator (DRBG) to generate an odd-parity key.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<18#Key Exchange Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<28#Visa Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 18 |\n| 1 | Key Exchange Key | 16, 32 | The KEK encrypted under variant zero of the MFK. This key |\nencrypts the randomly generated Visa Working Key. Visa\nrefers to the KEK as a Zone Control Master Key (ZCMK). This\nfield can contain 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a\nvolatile table location.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 28 |\n| 1 | Visa Working Key | 16 | The Visa Working Key encrypted under the Key Exchange |\nKey. The host application sends this cryptogram to the\nremote node. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 2 | Visa Working Key | 16 | The Visa Working Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK |\nspecified in field 1 of the command. The host application\nstores this cryptogram on its key database for subsequent\nuse. This field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Check Digits | 6 | The Visa Working Key check digits are the leftmost six |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Visa Working Key.\nUsage Notes\n Generate the KEK.\n\n\n<!-- Page 177 -->\n\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES\nKey (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\nThis command generates a random value, your results will be different.\n Clear-text Key Exchange Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Key Exchange Key encrypted under variant 0 of the MFK: 9007 B875 1BB7 AB4E\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<18#9007B8751BB7AB4E#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<28#EA3310FF19DB4F4C#6CE476EF7B6E4776#7DE170#>\n```\n\n\n"
