    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n\n- **Command ID:** `19`\n- **Title:** Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n- **PDF Pages:** 178 - 179\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 178 -->\n\n19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\nCommand 19 translates a Working Key from Base Key encryption (without a variant) to MFK encryption for\nlocal storage and subsequent use. This command imports a Working Key from a network that does not use\nAtalla variants.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<19#Variant#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<29#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 19 |\n| 1 | Variant | 1, 2 | The MFK variant which encrypts the Base Key.This field |\ncontains a decimal number in the range of 0 - 31. See\n“Variant” on page 59 for a list of supported variants.\n| 2 | Base Key | 16, 32 | The Base Key encrypted under variant of the MFK specified |\nin field 1. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal\ncharacters, or a volatile table location.\n| 3 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field |\ncontains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 29 |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK |\nspecified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 or\n32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Option 65 must be enabled if command field 1 contains the number 0.\n\n\n<!-- Page 179 -->\n\n Encrypt the Base Key under the appropriate variant of the MFK.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Variant: 1\n Clear-text Base Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Base Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86 D417 E64E 07E0\n Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: FEDC BA98 7654 3210\nThe PIN encryption key encrypted under the Base Key: 12C6 26AF 058B 433B\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<19#1#AE86D417E64E07E0#12C626AF058B433B#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<29#BC62A2AD72516EA1#A68C#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n\n- **Command ID:** `19`\n- **Title:** Translate Working Key for Local Storage\n- **PDF Pages:** 178 - 179\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 178 -->\n\n19 - Translate Working Key for Local Storage\nCommand 19 translates a Working Key from Base Key encryption (without a variant) to MFK encryption for\nlocal storage and subsequent use. This command imports a Working Key from a network that does not use\nAtalla variants.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\n| Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<19#Variant#Base Key#Working Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<29#Working Key#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 19 |\n| 1 | Variant | 1, 2 | The MFK variant which encrypts the Base Key.This field |\ncontains a decimal number in the range of 0 - 31. See\n“Variant” on page 59 for a list of supported variants.\n| 2 | Base Key | 16, 32 | The Base Key encrypted under variant of the MFK specified |\nin field 1. This field contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal\ncharacters, or a volatile table location.\n| 3 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the Base Key. This field |\ncontains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 29 |\n| 1 | Working Key | 16, 32 | The Working Key encrypted under the variant of the MFK |\nspecified in field 1 of the command. This field contains 16 or\n32 hexadecimal characters.\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The Working Key check digits are the leftmost four |\nhexadecimal characters that result from encrypting zeros\nunder the Working Key. If option 88 is enabled, the leftmost\nsix check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n Option 65 must be enabled if command field 1 contains the number 0.\n\n\n<!-- Page 179 -->\n\n Encrypt the Base Key under the appropriate variant of the MFK.\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Variant: 1\n Clear-text Base Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Base Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK: AE86 D417 E64E 07E0\n Clear-text PIN Encryption Key: FEDC BA98 7654 3210\nThe PIN encryption key encrypted under the Base Key: 12C6 26AF 058B 433B\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<19#1#AE86D417E64E07E0#12C626AF058B433B#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<29#BC62A2AD72516EA1#A68C#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
