      "es": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n- **PDF Pages:** 304 - 305\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 304 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Outgoing PIN Block | 16 | The PIN/Pad PIN Block encrypted under the Outgoing PIN |\nEncryption Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal\ncharacters.\nWhen a PIN sanity error is detected, the value in this field\nmay not be correct.\n| 2 | Sanity Check Indicator | 1 | The sanity check indicator. Option 4B specifies the type of |\nPIN sanity test to be performed on the incoming PIN block.\nThis field can contain one uppercase character, where:\nY = PIN block passes the sanity check\nN = PIN failed the sanity test. Or the length of the PIN is\nout of range and PIN-length error reporting has not\nbeen enabled. See “PIN sanity error” on page 73 and\noption “A1” on page 1415\nL = The length of the PIN is out of range.\nUsage Notes\n When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption\nKey is not equal-to or greater- than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key.\n When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response.\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 4455445544554455\nThe incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:\n72E7AEF691471872\n Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: 2233223322332233\nThe outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:\n8C2A7691A708A88D\n Encrypted PIN block: FBBAA4940B07C982\n Incoming pad character: X\n ANSI PAN Digits: 999999000000\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<33#31#72E7AEF691471872#8C2A7691A708A88D#FBBAA4940B07C982#X#999999000000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<43#2C39AECDB8EA47EC#Y#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 305 -->\n\n33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to PIN/Pad\nCommand 33 translates an encrypted PIN/Pad PIN block from encryption under an Incoming PIN\nEncryption Key encryption to encryption under an Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. The outgoing PIN block is a\nPIN/Pad PIN block.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n| <33#33#Incoming | PIN   Encryption |  | Key#Outgoing   PIN   Encryption   Key#PIN   Block# |\nIncoming Pad#Outgoing Pad#>\nResponse\n| <43#Outgoing PIN | Block#Sanity | Check | Indicator#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 33 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is PIN Pad. The format |\nof the outgoing PIN block is PIN Pad.\n| 2 | Incoming PIN Encryption | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. |\nKey This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field\ncontains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\nHeaders Supported: 3DES MFK\n1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N.\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n16, 32 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1\nof the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This\nfield contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n\n- **Command ID:** `33`\n- **Title:** Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to ANSI\n- **PDF Pages:** 304 - 305\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 304 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Outgoing PIN Block | 16 | The PIN/Pad PIN Block encrypted under the Outgoing PIN |\nEncryption Key. This field contains 16 hexadecimal\ncharacters.\nWhen a PIN sanity error is detected, the value in this field\nmay not be correct.\n| 2 | Sanity Check Indicator | 1 | The sanity check indicator. Option 4B specifies the type of |\nPIN sanity test to be performed on the incoming PIN block.\nThis field can contain one uppercase character, where:\nY = PIN block passes the sanity check\nN = PIN failed the sanity test. Or the length of the PIN is\nout of range and PIN-length error reporting has not\nbeen enabled. See “PIN sanity error” on page 73 and\noption “A1” on page 1415\nL = The length of the PIN is out of range.\nUsage Notes\n When option 49 is enabled, an error response is returned if the length of the Outgoing PIN Encryption\nKey is not equal-to or greater- than the length of the Incoming PIN Encryption Key.\n When either option 46 or 47 is enabled, the HSM will return an error response.\nExample\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A.\nSee “2key-3DES Key (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Clear-text incoming PIN Encryption Key: 4455445544554455\nThe incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:\n72E7AEF691471872\n Clear-text outgoing PIN Encryption Key: 2233223322332233\nThe outgoing PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1 of the MFK:\n8C2A7691A708A88D\n Encrypted PIN block: FBBAA4940B07C982\n Incoming pad character: X\n ANSI PAN Digits: 999999000000\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<33#31#72E7AEF691471872#8C2A7691A708A88D#FBBAA4940B07C982#X#999999000000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<43#2C39AECDB8EA47EC#Y#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 305 -->\n\n33 - Translate PIN, PIN/Pad to PIN/Pad\nCommand 33 translates an encrypted PIN/Pad PIN block from encryption under an Incoming PIN\nEncryption Key encryption to encryption under an Outgoing PIN Encryption Key. The outgoing PIN block is a\nPIN/Pad PIN block.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Disabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n| <33#33#Incoming | PIN   Encryption |  | Key#Outgoing   PIN   Encryption   Key#PIN   Block# |\nIncoming Pad#Outgoing Pad#>\nResponse\n| <43#Outgoing PIN | Block#Sanity | Check | Indicator#>[CRLF] |\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 33 |\n| 1 | 33 | 1 | The format of the incoming PIN block is PIN Pad. The format |\nof the outgoing PIN block is PIN Pad.\n| 2 | Incoming PIN Encryption | 74 | The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under the MFK. |\nKey This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This field\ncontains 74 printable ASCII characters, or a volatile table\nlocation.\nHeaders Supported: 3DES MFK\n1PUN*000, 1PUD*000, where * = E or N.\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3PUN*000, 3PUD*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n16, 32 The incoming PIN Encryption Key encrypted under variant 1\nof the MFK. This key encrypted the incoming PIN block. This\nfield contains 16 or 32 hexadecimal characters, or a volatile\ntable location.\n\n"
