      "es": "# Command 71 - Delete Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `71`\n- **Title:** Delete Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 498 - 499\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 498 -->\n\n71 - Delete Volatile Table Value\nCommand 71 deletes a value in a specific location within a section of the volatile table.\nReference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<71#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<81#Available Locations#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 71 |\n| 1 | Location | 1 - 4 | The location to be deleted. When deleting a value from |\nsection 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n0999. When deleting a row of a Diebold Number Table from\nsection 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n9999.\n1 - 4 The location to be deleted. This field contains a number in\nthe range of 0000 - 0999.\n| 2 | [Table Section#] | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section |\nof the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where:\n0 = DES key or conversion table section\n1 = Diebold Number Table section\nWhen this field is not present, the volatile table section is\nsection 0.\n[0] This field must not exist\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 81 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 499 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Remaining Locations | 4 | The number of locations available after this command is |\nexecuted. This field contains a number in the range of 0000\nthrough 0998.\n4 The number of locations available after this command is\nexecuted. This field contains a number in the range of 0000\nthrough 9998.\nExamples\nThe following example illustrates deleting a value stored in location 35 of section 0.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#35#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#0999#>\n```\n\nThe following example illustrates deleting a value stored in location 437 of section 1.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#437#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#2743#>\n```\n\nVariant Example\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<71#35#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<81#9999#>\n```\n\n\n",
