      "es": "# Command 72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `72`\n- **Title:** Verify Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 500 - 502\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 500 -->\n\n72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\nCommand 72 retrieves the check digits for the value stored in a specific location within a section of the\nvolatile table.\nReference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<72#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<82#Remaining Locations#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 72 |\n| 1 | Location | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. When verifying a value from |\nsection 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n0999. When verifying a row of a Diebold Number Table from\nsection 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n9999.\n1 - 4 The location to be verified. This field contains a number in\nthe range of 0000 - 0999.\n| 2 | [Table Section#] | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section |\nof the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where:\n0 = DES key or conversion table section\n1 = Diebold Number Table section\nWhen this field is not present, the volatile table section is\nsection 0.\n[0] This field must not exist\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 82 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 501 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Remaining Locations | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a |\nnumber in the range of 0000 - 0998.\n4 The number of locations available. This field contains a\nnumber in the range of 0000 - 9998.\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row |\ncheck digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters\nthat result from encrypting zeros under the key, conversion\ntable, or Diebold Number Table row. If option 88 is enabled,\nthe leftmost six check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n The HSM returns an error message <00#0701...> when the specified location is empty.\n For AKB and Variant key types, the following personality distinctions apply:\nAKB usage notes Variant usage notes\n2key-3DES (double-length) keys are loaded in two\nconsecutive locations within the table. When\nverifying a 2key-3DES (double-length) key, indicate\nthe first of the two locations. For example, if a\n2key-3DES (double-length) key is stored in\nlocations 3 and 4, specify location 3 to verify the\nentire key.\nAKB Examples\nVerify a DES key in location 17\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#17#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#1950#D5D4#>\n```\n\nVerify a row of a Diebold Number Table in location 438\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#438#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#9950#D5D4#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 502 -->\n\nVariant Example\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#17#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#1950#D5D4#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\n\n- **Command ID:** `72`\n- **Title:** Verify Volatile Table Value\n- **PDF Pages:** 500 - 502\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 500 -->\n\n72 - Verify Volatile Table Value\nCommand 72 retrieves the check digits for the value stored in a specific location within a section of the\nvolatile table.\nReference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<72#Location#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<82#Remaining Locations#Check Digits#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 72 |\n| 1 | Location | 1 - 4 | The location to be verified. When verifying a value from |\nsection 0, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n0999. When verifying a row of a Diebold Number Table from\nsection 1, this field contains a number in the range of 0000 -\n9999.\n1 - 4 The location to be verified. This field contains a number in\nthe range of 0000 - 0999.\n| 2 | [Table Section#] | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section |\nof the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where:\n0 = DES key or conversion table section\n1 = Diebold Number Table section\nWhen this field is not present, the volatile table section is\nsection 0.\n[0] This field must not exist\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 82 |\n\n\n<!-- Page 501 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 1 | Remaining Locations | 4 | The number of locations available. This field contains a |\nnumber in the range of 0000 - 0998.\n4 The number of locations available. This field contains a\nnumber in the range of 0000 - 9998.\n| 2 | Check Digits | 4, 6 | The key, conversion table, or Diebold Number Table row |\ncheck digits are the leftmost four hexadecimal characters\nthat result from encrypting zeros under the key, conversion\ntable, or Diebold Number Table row. If option 88 is enabled,\nthe leftmost six check digits are returned.\nUsage Notes\n The HSM returns an error message <00#0701...> when the specified location is empty.\n For AKB and Variant key types, the following personality distinctions apply:\nAKB usage notes Variant usage notes\n2key-3DES (double-length) keys are loaded in two\nconsecutive locations within the table. When\nverifying a 2key-3DES (double-length) key, indicate\nthe first of the two locations. For example, if a\n2key-3DES (double-length) key is stored in\nlocations 3 and 4, specify location 3 to verify the\nentire key.\nAKB Examples\nVerify a DES key in location 17\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#17#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#1950#D5D4#>\n```\n\nVerify a row of a Diebold Number Table in location 438\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#438#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#9950#D5D4#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 502 -->\n\nVariant Example\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<72#17#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<82#1950#D5D4#>\n```\n\n\n"
