      "es": "# Command 73 - Clear Section of Volatile Table\n\n- **Command ID:** `73`\n- **Title:** Clear Section of Volatile Table\n- **PDF Pages:** 503 - 504\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 503 -->\n\n73 - Clear Section of Volatile Table\nCommand 73 clears a section of the volatile table.\nReference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION: Before sending this command, make sure no other host application is using the volatile table.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<73#[Table Section#]>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<83#OK#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 73 |\n| 1 | [Table Section#] | [1] | This field is optional. When present, it specifies the section |\nof the table. This field contains a decimal digit, where:\n0 = DES key or conversion table section\n1 = Diebold Number Table section\nWhen this field is not present, the volatile table section is\nsection 0.\n[0] This field must not exist\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 83 |\n| 1 | OK | 2 | The table has been cleared. |\n\n\n<!-- Page 504 -->\n\nAKB Examples\nThe following example illustrates clearing section 0 of the volatile table.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<73#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<83#OK#>\n```\n\nThe following example illustrates clearing section 1 of the volatile table.\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<73#1#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<83#OK#>\n```\n\nVariant Example\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<73#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<83#OK#>\n```\n\n\n",
