      "es": "# Command 74 - Load Diebold Number Table\n\n- **Command ID:** `74`\n- **Title:** Load Diebold Number Table\n- **PDF Pages:** 505 - 507\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 505 -->\n\n74 - Load Diebold Number Table\nCommand 74 loads one encrypted row of a Diebold Number Table into the volatile table.\nReference Information: Section 8, “Storing values in the volatile table.”\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<74#Location#[Key Usage]#Diebold Number Table Row#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<84#Location#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 74 |\n| 1 | Location | 4 | The location where the row will be stored. This field contains |\na number between 0000 and 9999.\n| 2 | [Key Usage] | 0 | This field should be empty. |\n16 The Intermediate Key encrypted under variant 0 of the MFK.\nThis key encrypts the rows of the Diebold Number Table.\nThis field contains 16 hexadecimal characters.\n| 3 | Diebold Number Table | 74 | The row of the Diebold Number Table encrypted under the |\nRow MFK. This field contains 74 printable ASCII characters.\nHeaders Supported: 3DES MFK\n1ndN*000, where * = E or N.\nHeaders Supported: AES MFK\n3ndN*000, where * = E, N, or S.\n16 The row of the Diebold Number Table encrypted under\nvariant 5 of the MFK. This field contains 16 hexadecimal\ncharacters.\n\n\n<!-- Page 506 -->\n\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 84 |\n| 1 | Location | 4 | This field contains the contents of command field 1. |\nUsage Notes\n A Diebold Number Table contains 512 characters. It is organized as 32 rows, each of which is 16\nhexadecimal characters. To load a Diebold Number Table, you must load each encrypted row using a\nseparate command 74, and specify consecutive volatile table locations.\n The specified location will be loaded regardless of its current contents.\nUsage Notes specific to Variant\nUse the Secure Configuration Assistant for Windows and the HSM to encrypt the Diebold Number Table\nrows. The following procedure describes the process:\n1. Input or generate the Intermediate Key.\na. Use the SCA's Calculate Cryptogram function to input or generate a 1key-3DES (single-length)\nIntermediate Key.\nb. Select Key for the Cryptogram Type.\nc. Select 0 for the variant.\nd. Complete the transaction and save the cryptogram to the SCA Data Table, record the cryptogram\nand the location.\n2. Encrypt a row of the Diebold Number Table\na. Use the SCA's Calculate Cryptogram function to input row1 of the Diebold Number Table. Select Key\nfor the Cryptogram Type.\nb. Select 0 for the variant.\nc. Select the KEK slot number location from step 1 above.\nd. Complete the transaction and record the KEK cryptogram.\nRepeat this step for the remaining 31 rows of the Diebold Number Table.\n3. Create a command 74 for each row of the DNT as follows:\n\n```\n<74#location#step 1d cryptogram#step 2D KEK cryptogram#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 507 -->\n\nAKB 3DES MFK Example\nThe 3key-3DES Master File Key is:\n2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check digits = B196. See “3key-3DES\nKey (Triple-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Volatile Table Location number: 350\n Clear-text row of the Diebold Number Table: C860 2A41 4D38 2C5B\nThe row of the Diebold Number Table in AKB format:\n1ndNE000,87A94104D5C5452C50838D4244ADE06B22864B12E6BCD638,3D6565A1AD6B7279\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<74#350##1ndNE000,87A94104D5C5452C50838D4244ADE06B22864B12E6BCD638,3D6565A1AD6\n```\n\nB7279#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<84#0350#>\n```\n\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF\nFEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component\nvalues.\n Volatile Table Location number: 350\n Clear-text row of the Diebold Number Table: C8602A414D382C5B\nThe row of the Diebold Number Table in AKB format:\n3ndNE000,BBA98584D4E3211EC39F09E67D191671A3E38AA6A629527E,481F007A1B5AD245\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<74#350##3ndNE000,BBA98584D4E3211EC39F09E67D191671A3E38AA6A629527E,481F007A1B5\n```\n\nAD245#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<84#0350#>\n```\n\nVariant Example\nThe 2key-3DES MFK is: 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2, check digits = 057A. See “2key-3DES\nKey (Double-Length)” on page 1374 for component values.\n Volatile Table Location number: 350\n Clear-text Intermediate Key: 0123 4567 89AB CDEF\nThe Intermediate Key encrypted under variant 0 of the MFK: 9007B8751BB7AB4E\n Clear-text row of the Diebold Number Table: C860 2A41 4D38 2C5B\nThe row of the Diebold Number Table encrypted under variant 5 of the Intermediate Key:\n2144ADC8498E6920\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<74#350#9007B8751BB7AB4E#2144ADC8498E6920#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<84#0350#>\n```\n\n\n",
