      "es": "# Command 7C - Symmetric Key Size\n\n- **Command ID:** `7C`\n- **Title:** Symmetric Key Size\n- **PDF Pages:** 508 - 510\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 508 -->\n\n7C - Symmetric Key Size\nCommand 7C allows auditors and individuals in other capacities to find out the actual length of a key\nwrapped in an AKB block. This feature is useful for checking compliance with key size mandates.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION:\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Enabling this command allows anyone with access to the HSM (such as insiders, malware) to determine the\n> [!CAUTION]\n> keys that are most vulnerable to cryptanalysis. Users are cautioned that single-DES keys are vulnerable to key\n> [!CAUTION]\n> search at trivial cost, so allowing an attacker to pinpoint vulnerable keys is a significant risk.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Utimaco recommends careful analysis of the security tradeoffs of enabling this command.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<7C#Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<8C#Length#Check Digits#>\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 7C |\n| 1 | Key | Variable | The symmetric key encrypted under the MFK. This |\ncommand should support all symmetric working key\nheaders (version 1 and version 3).\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 8C |\n1 Length in bytes The length of the key in bytes. For example, a single-DES\nkey will return a value of 8. TDES keys are 16 or 24. AES\nkeys are 16, 24, or 32. HMAC keys may vary.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n\n<!-- Page 509 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n2 Check digits The check digits of the symmetric key.\n TDES key: check digits are the leftmost 6 digits\ncalculated by encrypting 0 with the key.\n AES key: check digits are the leftmost 10 digits of the\nCMAC of all zeros.\n HMAC key: check digits are the leftmost 14 digits of the\nSHA-256 hash of the KMAC key.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nUsage Notes\n When option EE is enabled, the AKB length of the AES or HMAC Working Key supplied in command field\n1 may be 110 characters.\nAKB 3DES MFK Example\n3key-3DES Master File Key = 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check\ndigits = B196. See Table A-2, 3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length) for component values.\n Clear-text DES working key = 3333 3333 3333 3333, check digits = ADC67D\n Working key in AKB format =\n1PUNE000,648CC44390726074BA90F7D2EB760D1D3BCDE456C1FA7915,4B8EF70DF76A5C9D\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<7C#1PUNE000,648CC44390726074BA90F7D2EB760D1D3BCDE456C1FA7915,4B8EF70DF76A5C9D\n```\n\n#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<8C#8#ADC67D#>\n```\n\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF\nFEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component\nvalues.\n Clear-text DES working key = 3333333333333333, check digits = ADC67D\n Working key in AKB format =\n3PUNE000,09F0C618F35FCDB8729715D61092B92B9554B066CD04C8DC,C9E6FCE5D702F7F4\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<7C#3PUNE000,09F0C618F35FCDB8729715D61092B92B9554B066CD04C8DC,C9E6FCE5D702F7F4\n```\n\n#>\n\n\n<!-- Page 510 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<8C#8#ADC67D#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 7C - Symmetric Key Size\n\n- **Command ID:** `7C`\n- **Title:** Symmetric Key Size\n- **PDF Pages:** 508 - 510\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 508 -->\n\n7C - Symmetric Key Size\nCommand 7C allows auditors and individuals in other capacities to find out the actual length of a key\nwrapped in an AKB block. This feature is useful for checking compliance with key size mandates.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> CAUTION:\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Enabling this command allows anyone with access to the HSM (such as insiders, malware) to determine the\n> [!CAUTION]\n> keys that are most vulnerable to cryptanalysis. Users are cautioned that single-DES keys are vulnerable to key\n> [!CAUTION]\n> search at trivial cost, so allowing an attacker to pinpoint vulnerable keys is a significant risk.\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Utimaco recommends careful analysis of the security tradeoffs of enabling this command.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Disabled 3DES, AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<7C#Key#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<8C#Length#Check Digits#>\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 7C |\n| 1 | Key | Variable | The symmetric key encrypted under the MFK. This |\ncommand should support all symmetric working key\nheaders (version 1 and version 3).\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | 8C |\n1 Length in bytes The length of the key in bytes. For example, a single-DES\nkey will return a value of 8. TDES keys are 16 or 24. AES\nkeys are 16, 24, or 32. HMAC keys may vary.\nLegal Characters: 0-9\n\n\n<!-- Page 509 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n2 Check digits The check digits of the symmetric key.\n TDES key: check digits are the leftmost 6 digits\ncalculated by encrypting 0 with the key.\n AES key: check digits are the leftmost 10 digits of the\nCMAC of all zeros.\n HMAC key: check digits are the leftmost 14 digits of the\nSHA-256 hash of the KMAC key.\nLegal Characters: 0-9, A-F\nUsage Notes\n When option EE is enabled, the AKB length of the AES or HMAC Working Key supplied in command field\n1 may be 110 characters.\nAKB 3DES MFK Example\n3key-3DES Master File Key = 2ABC 3DEF 4567 0189 9810 7645 FED3 CBA2 0123 4567 89AB CDEF, check\ndigits = B196. See Table A-2, 3key-3DES Key (Triple-Length) for component values.\n Clear-text DES working key = 3333 3333 3333 3333, check digits = ADC67D\n Working key in AKB format =\n1PUNE000,648CC44390726074BA90F7D2EB760D1D3BCDE456C1FA7915,4B8EF70DF76A5C9D\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<7C#1PUNE000,648CC44390726074BA90F7D2EB760D1D3BCDE456C1FA7915,4B8EF70DF76A5C9D\n```\n\n#>\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<8C#8#ADC67D#>\n```\n\nAKB AES MFK Example\nThe AES Master File Key is: 2ABC3DEF45670189 98107645FED3CBA2 0123456789ABCDEF\nFEDCBA9876543210, check digits = B9BCAB7B62. See “AES Key (256-bit)” on page 1374 for component\nvalues.\n Clear-text DES working key = 3333333333333333, check digits = ADC67D\n Working key in AKB format =\n3PUNE000,09F0C618F35FCDB8729715D61092B92B9554B066CD04C8DC,C9E6FCE5D702F7F4\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<7C#3PUNE000,09F0C618F35FCDB8729715D61092B92B9554B066CD04C8DC,C9E6FCE5D702F7F4\n```\n\n#>\n\n\n<!-- Page 510 -->\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<8C#8#ADC67D#>\n```\n\n\n"
