    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 9A - AKB Header Mapping\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** AKB Header Mapping\n- **PDF Pages:** 566 - 568\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 566 -->\n\n9A - AKB Header Mapping\nThis command accepts an AKB header and returns the corresponding version D header from TR-31.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#AKB Header#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#[TR-31 Header]#Exportability Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | AKB Header | 8 | The AKB Header to map to TR-31 header. |\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | [TR-31 Header] | 0, 16, | The version D header corresponding to the input header. If |\n32, 40 the header only has a mapping using the Atalla proprietary\nblock, then that block is included in the header. If response\nfield 3 = 4, then this field will be empty.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n\n<!-- Page 567 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 3 | Exportability Status | 1 | Indicates if a key with the input header could be exported |\ngiven the current security settings of the HSM.\n0 - Header is exportable.\n1 - Header is marked non-exportable. You cannot export a\nkey with this header, but you may be able to generate\nand export a key with this header.\n2 - Header cannot be exported because of option E1\nsettings.\n3 - Header cannot be exported because of the contents of\nthe settings_x.prm file under the AT41_EXPORT key\nword.\nThe response will not indicate if more than one reason\napplies. For example, if Option E1 = \"PMD\" and you try to\nexport a key with header 1KDNN000, this command will\nreturn '1' indicating the KEK is nonexportable and will\nnot check that the header also fails the E1 test.\n4 - Header cannot be exported via TR-31 commands\nbecause there is no supported mapping between the\nAKB header and TR-31. Response field 2 will be empty.\nLegal Characters: 0-4\nUsage Notes\n Note that the TR-31 header returned in the response will vary from the actual value returned from\ncommand 311 in three ways:\n This command will not include the length of the final key block. Instead, bytes 1-4 of the header will\nbe filled with zeros.\n This command will not allow the user to specify any optional header blocks.\n This command will let you know if a key with this header would be exportable given the current\nconfiguration of the HSM.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3PUNE000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000P0TB00E0000#0#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#1PUNN0I0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000K0TD00N02004112Atalla1PUNN0I0PB0E0000000000#1#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 568 -->\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3M2NS000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000M7HC00S0200HM0621PB0A000000#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 9A - AKB Header Mapping\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** AKB Header Mapping\n- **PDF Pages:** 566 - 568\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 566 -->\n\n9A - AKB Header Mapping\nThis command accepts an AKB header and returns the corresponding version D header from TR-31.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\nCommand\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#AKB Header#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#[TR-31 Header]#Exportability Status#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | AKB Header | 8 | The AKB Header to map to TR-31 header. |\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | AKB2TR31 | 8 | AKB2TR31 |\n| 2 | [TR-31 Header] | 0, 16, | The version D header corresponding to the input header. If |\n32, 40 the header only has a mapping using the Atalla proprietary\nblock, then that block is included in the header. If response\nfield 3 = 4, then this field will be empty.\nLegal Characters: Printable ASCII\n\n\n<!-- Page 567 -->\n\n\n### Response description (Continued)\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 3 | Exportability Status | 1 | Indicates if a key with the input header could be exported |\ngiven the current security settings of the HSM.\n0 - Header is exportable.\n1 - Header is marked non-exportable. You cannot export a\nkey with this header, but you may be able to generate\nand export a key with this header.\n2 - Header cannot be exported because of option E1\nsettings.\n3 - Header cannot be exported because of the contents of\nthe settings_x.prm file under the AT41_EXPORT key\nword.\nThe response will not indicate if more than one reason\napplies. For example, if Option E1 = \"PMD\" and you try to\nexport a key with header 1KDNN000, this command will\nreturn '1' indicating the KEK is nonexportable and will\nnot check that the header also fails the E1 test.\n4 - Header cannot be exported via TR-31 commands\nbecause there is no supported mapping between the\nAKB header and TR-31. Response field 2 will be empty.\nLegal Characters: 0-4\nUsage Notes\n Note that the TR-31 header returned in the response will vary from the actual value returned from\ncommand 311 in three ways:\n This command will not include the length of the final key block. Instead, bytes 1-4 of the header will\nbe filled with zeros.\n This command will not allow the user to specify any optional header blocks.\n This command will let you know if a key with this header would be exportable given the current\nconfiguration of the HSM.\nExamples\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3PUNE000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000P0TB00E0000#0#>\n```\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#1PUNN0I0#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000K0TD00N02004112Atalla1PUNN0I0PB0E0000000000#1#>\n```\n\n\n\n<!-- Page 568 -->\n\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#AKB2TR31#3M2NS000#>\n```\n\nThe HSM returns this response:\n\n```\n<AA#AKB2TR31#D0000M7HC00S0200HM0621PB0A000000#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
