    "markdownDoc": {
      "es": "# Command 9A - HSM DIAGTEST\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** HSM DIAGTEST\n- **PDF Pages:** 575 - 576\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 575 -->\n\n9A - HSM DIAGTEST\nCommand 9A – This command performs a cryptographic self-test on the HSM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<9A#DIAGTEST#Algorithm#[Perform All Flag]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<AA#Result#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | DIAGTEST | 8 | This field contains the word DIAGTEST. |\n| 2 | Algorithm | 1- 5 | This field contains a decimal value which specifies the test |\nto be performed, where:\n0 = All tests\n1 = 3DES known answer test\n2 = Random Number Generation test\n3 = RSA known answer test\n4 = MD5 known answer test\n5 = SHA-1 known answer test\n6 = SHA-2 known answer test\n7 = Kernel/Image test\n8 = AES known answer test\n9 = HMAC_SHA256 known answer test\n10 = HMAC-SHA1 known answer test\n11 = SHA512 known answer test\n12 = AES GCM and CMAC known answer test\n13 = ECC algorithm tests\n14 = KDF known answer test\nLeading zeros are allowed, but not required.\nFor example, 0 - 12 and 00000 - 00012 are valid values.\n| 3 | [Perform All Flag] | 0, 1, 2 | This field is only relevant when field 2 = 0. |\nWhen field 2 = 0 and this field is empty, the HSM will\nperform algorithm tests 1, 2, and 4 - 12, and 14.\nWhen field 2 = 0 and this field contains a value in the range\nof 1 - 99, the HSM will perform all algorithm tests.\n\n\n<!-- Page 576 -->\n\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | Result | 2, | When the test passes, this field contains the word OK. |\nVariable When a test fails this field contains the name of the failed\ntest.\nUsage Notes\n The test results are recorded in the system log.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#DIAGTEST#0#1#>\n```\n\nWhen the test completes successfully, the HSM returns the following response:\n\n```\n<AA#OK#>\n```\n\n\n",
      "en": "# Command 9A - HSM DIAGTEST\n\n- **Command ID:** `9A`\n- **Title:** HSM DIAGTEST\n- **PDF Pages:** 575 - 576\n\n---\n\n\n<!-- Page 575 -->\n\n9A - HSM DIAGTEST\nCommand 9A – This command performs a cryptographic self-test on the HSM.\n| Key Type |  | Default Setting | MFK Type |\nAKB Enabled 3DES, AES\n| 🟪 Variant |  | Enabled | 3DES |\nCommand\n\n```\n<9A#DIAGTEST#Algorithm#[Perform All Flag]#>\n```\n\nResponse\n\n```\n<AA#Result#>[CRLF]\n```\n\n\n### Command description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Command identifier | 2 | 9A |\n| 1 | DIAGTEST | 8 | This field contains the word DIAGTEST. |\n| 2 | Algorithm | 1- 5 | This field contains a decimal value which specifies the test |\nto be performed, where:\n0 = All tests\n1 = 3DES known answer test\n2 = Random Number Generation test\n3 = RSA known answer test\n4 = MD5 known answer test\n5 = SHA-1 known answer test\n6 = SHA-2 known answer test\n7 = Kernel/Image test\n8 = AES known answer test\n9 = HMAC_SHA256 known answer test\n10 = HMAC-SHA1 known answer test\n11 = SHA512 known answer test\n12 = AES GCM and CMAC known answer test\n13 = ECC algorithm tests\n14 = KDF known answer test\nLeading zeros are allowed, but not required.\nFor example, 0 - 12 and 00000 - 00012 are valid values.\n| 3 | [Perform All Flag] | 0, 1, 2 | This field is only relevant when field 2 = 0. |\nWhen field 2 = 0 and this field is empty, the HSM will\nperform algorithm tests 1, 2, and 4 - 12, and 14.\nWhen field 2 = 0 and this field contains a value in the range\nof 1 - 99, the HSM will perform all algorithm tests.\n\n\n<!-- Page 576 -->\n\n\n### Response description\n\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\nColors specific to key management method: No color = AKB & Variant = AKB = Variant\n| Field | Contents | Length | Description |\n| 0 | Response identifier | 2 | AA |\n| 1 | Result | 2, | When the test passes, this field contains the word OK. |\nVariable When a test fails this field contains the name of the failed\ntest.\nUsage Notes\n The test results are recorded in the system log.\nExample\nThe command looks like this:\n\n```\n<9A#DIAGTEST#0#1#>\n```\n\nWhen the test completes successfully, the HSM returns the following response:\n\n```\n<AA#OK#>\n```\n\n\n"
    },
